#passage(("This fellow left Islam without knowing Islam, apparently didn't really have much proof for [Islam]. And this is what happens with a lot of Christian [Prince's] callers. They don't even know [why] they're Muslims, and all it takes is a couple of arguments, a couple of Lies and statements like \"Why are you a Muslim? [Denounce] this,\" a bit of pressure, and that's it for them. And notice what caused him to become a Christian. Was there any proof that led him to Christianity? Were there any arguments? It's just \"I invite you to accept my Lord and Savior Jesus Christ\", and that's it. And these people, they're that fickle. They're just going with the flow. And all it's gonna take is someone to challenge this guy's [belief]. It's just gonna take a three-minute conversation, five [minute] conversation, and he's gonna switch to something else. And this is the danger. I wrote a little tweet earlier today saying something along the lines of: ask yourself \"Why am I Muslim?\" before someone asks you \"Why are you a Muslim?\" If you don't have a good answer to your question, then you're gonna have a crisis when you're asked this question.",), "Farid Responds, “Christian Prince Tricks Man Out of Islam [Lies #57-59]”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vUIm5Yhf96A", ((688, "11:28–13:09"),), id: 3166)
