#passage(("Now, we as human beings, why are we in this life? According to the Quran, we're being tested right now. If I'm being tested, if I'm following Allah, I'm following the [Prophetﷺ], and then I get misguided by Satan... The [Prophetﷺ] himself: Allah says in the Quran, if we did not keep you firm (who is Allah talking to? To the prophet sallallahu alaihi wasallam) you would incline towards the disbeliever a little bit. Allah is talking to the prophet. So now you have an example of a normal human being, your friend, my sister, my mother, whoever it is, some random person. You can spend your whole life trying to learn. That doesn't mean that you're not going to get deviated. You're going to get away from the path and you become misguided.", "The companion of the prophet, he said: if you're going to take someone as an example, let him take an example of someone who is dead. The person who's alive, he can be misguided. So you can say yes, the sister can be a great, perfect sister, awesome sister, but at one point she got misguided through something. Let's say the sister was influenced by a very clear ideology that exists in the west today called feminism, which are influencing the sisters, the women; liberalism are influencing our communities. I'm not saying you are, I'm not saying she is, but if we think that we as people who live, and these ideologies around us everywhere, in Hollywood, in YouTube, everywhere, and we don't get influenced by it, then we're deceiving ourselves. Anyone can get influenced by any ideology.", "I'm giving a hypothetical example. So someone was influenced by that. Let's say: okay, I don't want to do this. I don't want to follow this. I don't want to do that. So that person can get misguided. That wouldn't mean that now Islam no longer teaches us the hijab. So we cannot follow anyone blindly. That's the thing according to the Quran.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Non-Hijabi Woman Confronts Muslim On The Hijab Not Being In The Quran! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BzefH8uharg", ((405, "6:45–7:26"), (448, "7:28–8:18"), (502, "8:22–8:41"),), id: 3167)
