#passage(("Now you've seen a lot of proofs for the [prophethood] of rasulullah. However, maybe you don't have an answer to a specific argument against Islam. Keep in mind that there being some examples of arguments against Islam that you don't have an answer to yet doesn't mean that Islam is false. The proofs of [prophethood], that's where the fundamentals are at. If that clears out, then you can simply disregard individual arguments against Islam.", "Let's say that the prophet, peace be upon him, acted in a certain way that you're not too happy with. Let's take for example a narration that mentions something about the prophet, peace be upon him, himself and the way he acted, and deep down you feel that \"I can't swallow this, there seems to be a problem with this.\" Now maybe there's an issue with the hadith itself, maybe there's an issue with your morals and your standards, your values, maybe there's an issue with your understanding of the hadith. How are you supposed to deal with this? Well, as long as you know that the proofs of prophethood for rasulullah clear out, then you can simply disregard these individual issues that you may have. Now, I'm not saying don't look for answers. I strongly recommend that you do the research, ask people that have more knowledge than you. However, I want you to keep in mind once again: if all these proofs of prophethood clear out, then why is there any doubts? There shouldn't be any doubts.",), "Farid Responds, “Proofs of Prophethood 29: Final”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uyXilafWwg4", ((221, "3:41–4:12"), (252, "4:12–5:23"),), id: 3168)
// U FR304:152-181 | Farid Responds | 1
#passage(("So let's get back to the initial issue. You're having doubts in Islam and due to this you're going online to watch videos critiquing Islam even more. What if you find an answer? After searching for a while, you decide to watch another video critiquing Islam and you expose yourself to a new matter that you've never heard of, and the cycle is endless. You've been like that for days, maybe weeks, maybe months, and now you're just tired. If you want to get into refuting every single doubts, then I strongly recommend learning the Arabic language and familiarizing yourself with the classical texts. If you don't have the time or intention to do so, then I strongly recommend doing one thing, which is to solely focus on the proofs for Islam. You see, it's impossible for the proofs for and against Islam to both be correct. If the proofs that are for are correct, then by default the proofs against are going to be false. That's all you need to remember, and that is all you need to make all the petty arguments seem irrelevant.",), "Farid Responds, “\"I'm having doubts in Islam... What do I do?\"”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4KxQtb6Jzno", ((579, "9:39–11:23"),), id: 3169)

