#passage(("Sometimes you're not necessarily going to find the answers you're looking for. This has nothing to do with proofs for Islam per se, but it has to do with an Islamic matter that I just simply didn't have an answer to. And what I did was I contacted multiple [sheikhs], contacted a friend who was curious about the same issue, I read many books looking for an answer for this, and I simply couldn't find an answer. And one day I thought to myself: \"[Farid], maybe you're never gonna know, and just simply accept it.\" And one day, randomly, due to patience, I was rewarded. I was listening to an audio lecture that had nothing to do with the subject, and the first half hour of that audio lecture was dedicated to the questions that I had in mind. So subhanallah, I felt like it was a gift from God to me, to just satisfy my thirst for that answer.", "So once again, just because you do not have an answer at this moment doesn't mean that there is no answer, doesn't mean that you're not going to find an answer. And once again, as long as the proofs of prophethood hold, then the specific individual doubts are irrelevant.",), "Farid Responds, “Proofs of Prophethood 29: Final”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uyXilafWwg4", ((327, "5:27–6:36"), (400, "6:40–6:57"),), id: 3172)
