#passage(("My most important advice is, stop asking the wrong people about Islam. You cannot ask people like this person from \"Fresh and Fit\" or other people like Salim or these individuals who are not on the religion themselves; they're not practising Islam and they're not really familiar with the rules of Islam. So when you ask them questions about it, I think most of the time they'll give you answers that are incorrect, and you'd think that they are saying the truth. And you're also waiting for them, in a way, to encourage you to practice, while they themselves don't want to practice. So I think you should, offline (it doesn't have to be online), surround [yourself] with people who are actually practising Islam, people who encourage you, who go with you to the mosque, not going alone, because you will need company.", "Growing up with Islam means nothing if you did not practice it and left it. That means zero, nothing. The Companions of the Prophetﷺ, who we imitate and follow after the prophet, are all of them people who accepted Islam, people who accepted the religion and practice the religion in their life.", "Islam itself teaches you that religion is something that you ask the people who are specialised in these fields. Like, for example, when you have a heart operation or you got some pain, you're not going to go to one of your friends and ask him. People treat religion differently, somehow, for some reason, as if it is not a specialty. It is also a field of specialty that you would require certain people who at least done some sort of studying, investigation. So when you ask these questions they actually give you answers and give you reasoning and look at your situation as well, because sometimes even the answer that you give will be depending on the person's situation. It's not as simple as \"the Quran says that, therefore I'm going to say it to you.\" So they have to read you in a specific way, see where you are.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Muslim Lantern Gets Sneak∅ To Rethink His Views! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ocg_ABofNVU", ((3312, "55:12–55:47"), (3444, "57:24–57:37"), (3462, "57:42–58:20"),), id: 3192)
