#passage(("There is an interesting clip that I want to react to from this YouTuber, Asmongold. I invited him for a discussion, where he was saying that he would like to read the Quran and learn what Muslims actually believe. He actually did respond to this invitation. He said he appreciates it, but then he goes and says that he has Muslim friends: \"Yeah, I have Muslim friends and I'm going to ask them about it.\"", "Now, what is the issue with this? Just because someone is born into a faith or into a religion, it doesn't make them knowledgeable about it. The West is the best example of this. How many people are born into Christianity, and they just don't go to church and never read the Bible? \"Oh, I have Christian friends, so I'm going to ask them about Christianity.\" They're not familiar with the teachings of Christianity. So you'd go to someone who studied, who learned, and who is an expert in that field. And you don't have to talk to me, really. Asmongold doesn't have to talk to me. You can talk to any Muslim who is knowledgeable about Islam; that's all we're asking.", "So sadly, a lot of people are happy being in an echo chamber. They've never left America, they've never visited Muslim countries, they never saw what people actually believe. And they have an echo chamber of followers that are also Americans: \"America is the best country in the world. We are the advanced people in every field; we know everything.\" Some of them never left their mother's basement, let alone leave their country and see what other people believe in. It's sad when people live in echo chambers.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Asmongold Responds - Women Are Oppressed In Islam? | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sGEADBXUEFo", ((9, "0:09–1:08"), (70, "1:10–2:03"), (128, "2:08–2:37"),), id: 3194)
