#passage(("Should Muslims be asking religious questions to Artificial Intelligence? The answer is ABSOLUTELY NOT! We should not be doing that. Now, not only do you have this problem of biases, which is based on data input into the Artificial Intelligence, but you also have a bigger problem. And that bigger problem is the fact that it cannot differentiate the context of the person asking the question.", "What does that mean? We have an example in the Islamic tradition. In the Islamic tradition you have someone coming to one of the Sahaba (it was either 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas or 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud), and then he was asked: Can I kiss my wife while I'm fasting? We know that intercourse breaks your fast, but can you kiss your wife while you are fasting or not? So he gave an answer to the person who was asking him: no. And then another person came and asked the same question. Then he said to him: yes. So now he gave two different answers to the SAME exact question. Why? It's based on the context of the person asking the question. Now, ChatGPT does not ask you a question, collect information, and know your context before it gives you an answer.", "Why did the Companion give two different answers to the same question? Because one of them was an old man, so he can control his desire. That kiss that he can do while he's fasting is not going to lead him to doing intercourse, which can break his fast, which is a Major Sin. Now, the other person asking was young. So if he kisses his wife, maybe that would awaken his desire; maybe it will lead him to intercourse, which will break his fast. So, looking at the context here, different contexts: this person is old, this person is young; this person has more control over his desires, this person doesn't. It's the same question, but the answers are drastically different.", "So we need to understand the context of the person. Where are they at? You need to understand things gradually. You cannot just respond and give them answers like this. So you cannot rely on Chat GPT when it comes to Islamic knowledge and Islamic questions. You need to ask the people of knowledge, the scholars. You go to these people and you ask them about Islamic questions.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Can Muslims Really Trust Artificial Intelligence?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7opfbjHoB1E", ((379, "6:19–6:38"), (402, "6:42–7:19"), (442, "7:22–7:53"), (477, "7:57–8:14"),), id: 3205)

