#passage(("You don't need the hadith for now, because there's a lot of hadith; you have thousands of hadith, tens of thousands. This hadith is explaining the Quran, and [it's] given us the example of the prophet's life. If you want to fully understand the Quran, you want to become a Muslim, you start with the Quran. You first understand the Quran, [its] message; you see if you agree with it, you understand what its evidence is. Then, once you do that, you go to teachers and scholars who will explain to you the hadith. So that's more advanced for you: become a Muslim, and then we start explaining to you.", "Once you accept the Quran is from God, then you go into practicing your life bit by bit. No Muslim memorizes all the hadith and understands all of them. That's not requirement, because so many. What is requirement is what's to do with your day-to-day life: your beliefs and the things like how you pray, how you fast, whatever you want to engage in; that's what you need to learn about.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Lady Grills Muslim With Questions Then A Surprise Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JOpckbnPmsM", ((3410, "56:50–58:06"), (3494, "58:14–58:34"),), id: 3206)
