#passage(("For someone who comes from a Christian background, chapter 2 talks about Adam and his creation, and then the story of Adam, and then it goes into a description of Moses as well. There'll be a lot more familiar. I would say read it the way it is, in the order it is. And I don't agree with the lazy approach many people would want to take: just read the smaller. No. Read and take your time, finish reading, investigate, because the story there is way more different than Christianity. And the Christians base their whole religion on the original sin, and this original sin is completely refuted in the beginning of the Quran. So I wouldn't want to miss that for someone who has a Christian background, and tell him go read from the smaller chapters of the Quran that talk about the afterlife or the attributes of Allah.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Curious Canadian Grills Muslim With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XhEel3w9jYY", ((718, "11:58–12:40"),), id: 3208)
