#passage(("The point I was making is that the Bible is not preserved. Therefore you do not really know what Jesus said or didn't even say. If you do not know what Jesus said and didn't say, then there's no way you can come to a Muslim and say you guys are opposing Jesus or going against what Jesus taught. You don't even know what Jesus said.", "You said: I don't believe in the teachings of prophet Muhammad. What I mentioned to you, for example: (Love for others what you love for yourself). (There's no superiority of a black over a white or a white over a black). (You should take care of your family and daughter and you should be the best person towards your family). So you believe in the teachings of Prophet Muhammad. The thing is, you don't know the teachings. The point I'm making is this: you guys have not yet read what Islam says. You've not read the Quran, you do not know the life of the Prophetﷺ. All you know is what you've heard from your surroundings, from people who already have an agenda against Islam, which are lying. I gave you a clear example of this idea of Jewish woman cursing Prophet Muhammad for 6 months, which is not even in the Quran. No Muslim believes that. But the thing is, you hear these things from your surroundings.", "The difference is, I'm not a Christian, but I'm telling you what the Bible says. I know what the Bible says, because I've read it. I don't only know what the Bible says, but I know History and the Manuscripts and the names of the Manuscripts and their dates, because I'm not going to just sit here and claim I'm trying to learn while I've not even read your own Scripture.", "What I would say is: the minimum you can do personally, if you really want to know what the Prophet did, is to pick up the sources of Muslims: the Quran, and pick up a biography of Prophet and read his life. If you really want to know how he lived his life, I can recommend you different biographies. Read the biography of the life of the Prophetﷺ; it's available in English. Read the Quran; it's available in English, Spanish, depending on your language, available to read it in your language. And actually, you will KNOW. You're not going to say: \"I don't know.\" You'll say: I read and actually know now what Islam says, because I've read it myself.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Family Grills Muslim On His Beliefs! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TKqmYTyocyo", ((2231, "37:11–37:24"), (2311, "38:31–39:17"), (2361, "39:21–39:31"), (2388, "39:48–40:18"),), id: 3215)
// U ML278:840-892 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("My words of advice is that you pick up a copy of the Quran yourself, in the language that you prefer, and read it, and the biography of the Prophet, his life. Give it a shot, read it, see: is it actually what those people are telling you? Is it what you hear in the Media and all of these videos you see, which are fabricated, about those people killing these people? All of this nonsense, all of these things that they show you in the media trying to push you away from Islam. When you read the text itself, you think to yourself: is this actually the same thing that I'm hearing? Is this what people around me are telling me? And you yourself will come to the conclusion that they're lying to you. I'm not telling you to take my word. You'll come to your own conclusion, but just be sincere with it.", "All I wanted to do is this: we shouldn't be trusting the hear-saying, things we hear around the Discord servers and here and there, because those people have not educated themselves; they have an agenda, and they're spreading lies about things that they've not read, that they themselves don't know. Second thing is, we need to educate ourselves about other people's beliefs by reading their own sources, their own traditions, their own books, their own Quran, their own biographies, to see what these people actually believe. Because they don't believe from the servers; they believe the Quran that they themselves read, they believe the biography that they themselves read. So to understand them, I need to read what they read, to know what they actually believe. So this is all I wanted to do: to actually understand that there's a lot of lies around from the Media, and there's a reason for it. And there's a lot of attacks on Islam for a reason, because it's The Truth. And we should actually investigate ourselves and come to our own conclusions.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Family Grills Muslim On His Beliefs! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TKqmYTyocyo", ((2840, "47:20–48:13"), (2972, "49:32–50:13"),), id: 3216)
// U ML231:338-373 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("Even me, as an Arabic speaker, I have to go to other people; that's how research works. You go to the primary source materials and you read the information in the primary source materials. Now, if these primary source materials happen to be in a specific language, you're going to have to speak that language in order for you to understand that primary source material. For instance, if I want to study the primary source materials of the Greek Scriptures, I will have to read it in Greek, or read the translation of it into a language I understand. If I want to understand that primary source materials in Hebrew (in which they exist, in Hebrew and Greek, for the Old and New Testament, for example), I'll have to learn that language and understand it. That is with any religion; not even any religion, anything. If I want to learn the science primary source materials of what someone said in Latin in the 1900s, or whatever it is, or any time, I need to learn that language in order for me to understand what they're saying!", "No one has said you have to learn Arabic to be a Muslim. We are saying, if you want to go into specialised topics in which the primary source materials are in a specific language, of course you have to understand that language, or look what is the available material in that language which we can read in a translated language which we can understand. I didn't say you cannot find any book that can explain to you; there are books in English that are written that explain the history of the Quranic text. I believe al'Azmi has a book (A-L-A-Z-M-I, that's his name, al'Azmi), and he has a book, it's called The History of the Quranic Text, or something related to that. I'm sure if you put his name and you put that, you'll find, and it's available in English. I'm not saying this is the best book and has all of the information. You could still have questions after reading this book, which can be dealt with.", "But the point I'm making is: when you describe Ibn Kathir specifically, you're reading the abridged version of his translation, which has issues, because it's not the full context. It's not even a language thing. Not everything he said is there; some of what he said is there, which can change the meaning when I take something out of context. I just said, if you want to look at the specialised field, like all of these events, the preservation of the Quran: they happened at the time of the Prophet or after him, the first few hundred years, and the primary source materials are found in the Arabic language, because it was happening in a part of the world where people were speaking Arabic! So it would make sense for you to know the Arabic language to read the primary source material, or to read at least a correct, full context translation of the history of that event taking place.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Confronts Muslim On Quran Preservation! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HidefUs_Fak", ((1397, "23:17–24:08"), (1453, "24:13–25:01"), (1504, "25:04–25:48"),), id: 3217)
// U ML231:250-311 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("When you come asking an individual for answers and then say, I'm not going to take your answers, that is the definition of logical inconsistency. If you don't think I'm going to give you accurate answers, then it would not make any sense to ask me the question. When I say \"watch my video\", it's because you're coming and asking ME questions, so of course I'm going to recommend you to my work on the matter. In that video that I made, I mentioned the primary source material, I mentioned the sources, in which you can easily go and open and read if you want to read. So that is the point that I was making: you don't have to take my word for it. I bring the primary source materials to everything I say.", "When I say to you, you don't understand what Ibn Kathir says, it's not an insult to you. Whether you're reading it in English or German, whatever you're reading is a translation of a translation. Now, Ibn Kathir's full Tafseer is not available in English anyway. It's the abridged version of Ibn Kathir that is available in English. So when I say you're not understanding what Ibn Kathir says, it has nothing to do only with your reading comprehension skills. It has to do with it being a translation, and perhaps not full context of what he actually said.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Confronts Muslim On Quran Preservation! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HidefUs_Fak", ((1162, "19:22–20:00"), (1220, "20:20–21:07"),), id: 3218)
