#passage(("Remember, there are many more proofs of prophethood. What I did was I summarized some; well, again, not even all the arguments. Lovely book; it's two volumes long, by the way, and there's a lot more information here that I did not share. It is quite a heavy book, a lot of information, especially about differences among sects and history of the church; he goes into a lot of different topics. So there are a lot of other books [on proofs of prophethood]. Most of these works are classical works. And, by the way, just by going through the [Sirah] itself, a lot of it can be used as proof for the [prophethood] of rasulullah, even matters that don't seem to be that direct, like the way the prophet, peace be upon him, spoke to the kings of his time, and the way that he dealt with hypocrites, a lot of stuff like that, about his mannerisms as well. There are also some other classical works. These two books mention a lot of examples of things that you would find in previous scriptures about the prophet, peace be upon him. So those are also two highly recommended reads. What I find really interesting about these is a lot of these works focus on hadith-based argument for Islam, unlike [Abd al-Jabbar's] book, which simply focuses on rational proofs for Islam.",), "Farid Responds, “Proofs of Prophethood 29: Final”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uyXilafWwg4", ((5, "0:05–2:31"),), id: 3228)
