#passage(("This is a good channel. It's called ManyProphetsOneMessage. It has a good video about the Predictions of the Future. It's not my channel. \"The Quran and the Secrets of Babylon\": you can watch this one. This one: \"Mind blowing Prophecies of Prophet Muhammad\". They will have references as well. And there was something in Egypt, the Quran and ancient Egypt: \"The Quran and the Secrets of Egypt\". Watch these ones; it will give you References.", "This is Dr. Eyad Qunaibi. He's got a beautiful channel. Look at the videos that talk about Evolution. He has a big series. It's not all translated yet, but many of the episodes are translated. I think even the one about the genome, 99%: it's translated.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Challenges Muslim On Evolution! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hBuaweGxlDg", ((1414, "23:34–24:09"), (1464, "24:24–24:44"),), id: 3231)
// U ML239:3805-3843 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("It depends on the questioner: does the questioner speak Arabic, or does not speak Arabic, or does he speak just English? But the first thing I'm going to say is the Quran, the Quran. The Quran is the book that is [the Furqan], the differentiator between truth and false; Quran differentiates between truth and false. Now, there are books written from our righteous [predecessors]; there are many, many books. These are all, I'm saying, Arabic, but how many of them translate? You find some of these books translated in English, but these books have found some defects, some problems with it, sometimes in the translation. So it's best to have a teacher, if you don't speak Arabic.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Aqeedah (Creed) And Its Significance In Islam | AIM Conference 2024 NJ | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ULnwXbVf_cM", ((9086, "2:31:26–2:32:38"),), id: 3232)
// U ML233:2011-2046 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("What books or courses do you recommend for more productive [dawah], is the question. And the answer is that I always give, all the time: The Book of Allah. I see many people, they don't think about the Quran before they think about other books. How are you going to do [dawah] to that that you don't know? Books are always like things which are secondary, later on, branches; the fundamentals is the Quran. You memorize as much as you can. I always recomend [Tafsir as-Sa'di]. I believe two volumes; I don't know how many volumes, I'm not sure, but it's available translated in the English language for people to read. So the book of Allah first, and then, inshallah, you move to the [Sirah] and the Sunnah of the prophet, books like these.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Eddie @TheDeenShowTV Interviews The Muslim Lantern | Masjid Dar Al-Qur'an | Chicago - USA”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sLfJyJGj_eg", ((4387, "1:13:07–1:14:24"),), id: 3233)
