#passage(("I'll tell you about someone who's better than me and all of us and everyone, which is the Prophet Muhammadﷺ. Our question should be: how do we become like the Prophet Muhammadﷺ? Not like me or like anyone else, living today or living in the past, other than the Prophet Muhammadﷺ. What did I do? I implemented and learned and studied how the Prophet Muhammadﷺ behaved with the people, as much as I could. And my dawah is very deficient in comparison to the Prophet Muhammadﷺ; my manners are very deficient in comparison to the Prophet Muhammadﷺ. But anything good that you would see, if it's there, is from the Prophet Muhammadﷺ. So you study الشمائل المحمدية, the behavior of the Prophet Muhammadﷺ, his description, his Akhlaq, how he acted, how he behaved with people, how he gave dawah.", "And then you study the foundations of the religion, as we said, which will equip you with your 'Aqeeda, your fundamental creed. That's why the conference in New Jersey was about that. The 'Aqeeda, which is the creed, which is to believe in Allah, His books, His Messengers, these Articles of Faith and their details, because that's what people will ask you about. Whoever asks you a question, it would be one of these things. They either ask you about Allah, His names, His attributes, His existence, His worship; either they will ask you about the Prophets of God; they'll ask you about the Books; they'll ask you about the Day of Judgment. The questions will not exit these beliefs in 'Aqeeda; they'll not be more or less than this. This is what people will ask you. So, by you studying them properly, and understanding them, you will be able to answer most, if not all, of the questions that you come across, InshaAllah. So: behavior and manners from the Prophetﷺ, and the application; and knowledge, you seek it and you apply.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Islam Unveiled: Compelling Evidence For The Truthfulness Of Islam | Chicago - USA | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AUFsBco_CF0", ((4390, "1:13:10–1:13:48"), (4434, "1:13:54–1:14:47"),), id: 3234)

== 66. Dawah: methods, conduct and debates

=== 66.1 Dawah as conveying the message, not convincing
// NODE P15.C03.S01
#author("The Muslim Lantern")
// U ML162:1-53 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("As a Muslim, Allah tells us to deliver The Message. What is delivering The Message? Delivering The Message is like giving someone, for example, a piece of paper with information written on it, and the person reads it. Or telling him certain types of information.", "Everyone will die one day, and everyone will be held accountable for how they lived their life. That is a FACT from our worldview. If they accept Islam, it's for their own benefit. I don't need to convince anyone. That is the most important part that I want to make. So I'm not really like a salesman. I'm not coming with a piece of paper, like \"oh, please buy this paper!\"",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Heated Atheist Challenges A Muslim To Prove The Existence Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YGW_AhJHSQ4", ((68, "1:08–1:19"), (86, "1:26–1:56"),), id: 3235)
// U ML248:521-558 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("I remember one time going to the corner, and there's this new person there, and he's just saying things and making mistakes. And then I went to one of the brothers there who's more senior. I said, this person is making mistakes. Then what he ended up saying to me is: he's learning. You learn, then you give the [dawah]. So we've got this issue now today, that the people think that I'm going to learn through giving the [dawah].", "One thing I've learned from all of these years, the most important thing, I would say, is this idea: [dawah] is not about convincing the other person. This takes so much weight from your shoulder. You try to go spin around, use this argument, this philosophical argument, you're trying your best to convince someone; Allah did not give you that. He did not put that responsibility. Allah says you're not a controller over them. It's only upon the [messenger] to deliver the message.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Amazing Collab| The Muslim Lantern & Sheikh Uthman Meet For The First Time| @OneMessageFoundation”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LVdIHlFWDgc", ((1173, "19:33–19:57"), (1213, "20:13–20:47"),), id: 3236)
// U ML246:32-69 | The Muslim Lantern | 5
#passage(("The difference between Islam and any other faith –and I think that is very important for people to understand– in Islam, the job of us, or the job of the Messengers of God, or us trying to fulfil the same Message of the Messengers of God, is not to convince anyone. This is not the attitude that any Muslim takes towards Islam. The attitude that we take towards Islam is quite simple: it is delivering the Message. Allah says in the Quran (Al'ankabut29:18) وَمَا عَلَى ٱلرَّسُولِ إِلَّا ٱلْبَلَـٰغُ ٱلْمُبِينُ (It's only upon the Messenger to give a clear demonstration and delivery of the Message).", "So it's upon me as someone who is acting as a Messenger in this case –not a Messenger of God like the Prophets, no!– I'm just delivering the Message of the Messenger of God. So I'm just conveying what he said, because he said: (Convey upon me my Message to the people). So, we are conveying the Message of the Messenger of God, the Messenger of Allah.", "We say to the people that Allah has sent Prophets and Messengers. These Prophets and Messengers came at different times and different localities. They had one Message, which is that there is only One Entity worthy of worship. That Entity is not like us as humans; does not have children, does not have fathers, does not have grandfathers; created the universe and gives life and takes away life from people, causes death. And it created everything around us and placed us in this life as a test, that whatever we do here in this life is a test for us. And if we choose to do good –because the morality source is from that Creator, from that God, that He reveals it to us– and if we choose to do the good that He commanded us to do, it will be good for us in this life, and it will be good for us in the Afterlife. And if we choose to disobey, and to harm people, and we'll do evil, there will be consequences in the afterlife for these actions.", "So, this is essentially the Message of Islam. And these Prophets and Messengers bring revelation, and within that revelation there's the Guidance and teachings, telling you what will happen in the future, and what will happen to you when you die, etc. And we deliver that Message to the people. And this is our job as Muslims.", "But trying to convince people, I believe, is already an incorrect attitude to take to anything. People have to have a genuine interest in whatever it is that they're approaching. They have to have genuine interest, they have to be sincere, and they have to look and research. And then I believe anyone who's sincere, who's open-minded, when he opens the Quran and reads, he will recognize that what he's reading there are not human words, that's not a human being writing this information, because this is a very distinguished difference –especially for people who read– between how humans write and what they say, and how the Creator addresses and speaks to His creation.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Confronts Muslim On The Clarity Of The Quran! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ozeX5ELYDh0", ((90, "1:30–2:02"), (128, "2:08–2:21"), (145, "2:25–3:03"), (190, "3:10–3:22"), (206, "3:26–3:55"),), id: 3237)
