#refbox("Reference text: Quran 29:18, quran.com (Saheeh International)", (("29:18", "And if you [people] deny [the message] - already nations before you have denied. And there is not upon the Messenger except [the duty of] clear notification."),))
// U ML053:193-210 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("The uncle of the Prophet, he was told by the other people of Quraysh: remain on the religion of your forefathers. That was the last thing people told him before he died. Then he said OK, he's going to remain -on his deathbed- and he remained on it.", "Islam does NOT teach you to CONVINCE, Islam teaches you to CONVEY. The Truth is innate, and there will always be people who will reject the Truth knowing it is the Truth. But if you convey the Message, there's also sincere people, even if they think it's a part of the culture.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Arab Christian Shares His Experience With Islam And Christianity! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEUpYAh5b3E", ((623, "10:23–10:31"), (640, "10:40–10:56"),), id: 3238)
// U ML042:26-47 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("We're not asking anybody to believe. There's a difference between me being accessible, cuz that's my obligation as a Muslim, and me being a salesman. It's very important for you people to understand that. There's a difference between being accessible to the people, because if someone has a question, they're looking for someone to answer their questions. They're seekers. So, we need to be outlets for people. Now, you have salesmen, some religions with a microphone shouting and screaming in the middle of the streets. We don't do that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Intellectually Bankrupt Atheist Demands Evidence For God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UJamL35PCk8", ((51, "0:51–1:45"),), id: 3239)
// U ML240:229-253 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("I would rather more people know about Islam, even if they're not going to accept it. For a simple reason: they would understand I'm not something that they thought I was. You will realize they're more educated now about what Muslims are, [what] Muslims do, etc. So I would say that it's better, even if they don't accept Islam.", "Some people think our goal is to make the whole planet Muslims. We know for a fact that Allah told us there will be believers and disbelievers (Yunus10:99). Allah told us certain people will never accept Islam no matter how many signs you show them (Ala'raf7:132). We believe the prophets, the best of the messengers, came, and some of these prophets converted zero people, no one accepted Islam but them! Because guidance is in Allah's hand. But the delivery of the message is upon us, because there are sincere people who are looking, so it's a responsibility upon me to deliver the message. At least these people will take the message, and they're looking for it.", "Today, that woman that I told you accepted Islam, she said -word for word-: I'm looking for the purpose in life, I'm looking for guidance, I need someone to guide me. And if we're not there, Allah did not use us as a means, she'll go somewhere else. She'll go to the wrong people; she's looking for purpose.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The One Minute Podcast | Sneak∅ Interviews The Muslim Lantern | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8fgMbBAaheo", ((634, "10:34–10:47"), (652, "10:52–11:24"), (687, "11:27–11:41"),), id: 3240)
