#refbox("Reference text: Quran 10:99, quran.com (Saheeh International)", (("10:99", "And had your Lord willed, those on earth would have believed - all of them entirely. Then, [O Muḥammad], would you compel the people in order that they become believers?"),))
// R quran_007_132.json
#refbox("Reference text: Quran 7:132, quran.com (Saheeh International)", (("7:132", "And they said, \"No matter what sign you bring us with which to bewitch us, we will not be believers in you.\""),))
// U ML145:455-473 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("The reason we follow Islam, or we tell people about Islam, is because we can demonstrate this is from God, and then we tell people to follow God. But in the same time, Allah in the Quran tells us something very important (alQasas28:56): (we do not guide the people we love). And Allah tells us in the Quran (alBaqara2:256): (there is no compulsion in religion). So only to tell people the Truth; it's not upon me to guide anyone.", "Someone could listen, can like what I say, can follow it, and can dislike it, but like or dislike, based on their subjective upbringing, would it change the fact that it's objectively True? No! What they need to do is to be SINCERE with themselves, and analyse the evidence that are there.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Liberal Woman Debates Muslim On The Need For Religion! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kBJxu5UYcy4", ((1465, "24:25–24:49"), (1493, "24:53–25:06"),), id: 3241)
