// U ML006:881-897 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("Each of you here, you're sitting down, it's a very small town, further away from London. Probably have a lot more non-Muslims here than you do Muslims. You have a responsibility as well to deliver this message. You have neighbors, you have friends, you have colleagues, non-Muslims; you need to transmit this knowledge that you have. If you know you have the truth, you should have mercy for mankind, like the [prophet] was sent as a mercy to mankind. You don't want them to die and be in eternal hellfire. You want goodness and truth for them.", "Go to anybody, just present these criterias. Nobody will disagree with you rationally that if for a book to be from God, it has to say it's from God. They would not disagree with you that it has to be free from contradictions. So take this knowledge and put it into implementation, and invite people closer to [Allah].",), "The Muslim Lantern, “How Do You Know Which Religion Is From God? A Detailed Comprehensive Analysis | The Muslim Lantern”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9F5gS1yWIRI", ((3140, "52:20–52:53"), (3180, "53:00–53:15"),), id: 3242)
// U ML236:43-88 | The Muslim Lantern | 4
#passage(("Now the question is: how many of us, sitting down here today, are able to represent the Truth upon demand? Meaning, when someone comes to you, in a non-Muslim land, majority non-Muslim land, now the situations in which you can encounter people who can ask you, where is the proof that this is true? Where is the proof that this is from God? The likelihood is very high. The question is how many of us are able to present something? I'm not saying دليل (dalil); we're talking about Burhan.", "Now, it is incumbent upon us, especially living in a non-Muslim land, we have an obligation of Da'wah. And in this case, we have an obligation on every single person. Because usually da'wah is فرض كفاية, meaning it's a \"communal obligation\". But in this case, it is upon everyone, because the communal obligation is not being fulfilled. There are many people who have not heard anything about Islam, just what the media tells them about Islam. That's what they heard. They've not heard anything good about Islam. No one has given them the Message. Sometimes your neighbours, you've not talked to them. So it's upon us to deliver that Message, which means that it's also necessary that we know how to represent that Islam is the Truth. That's number one.", "And number two, is for yourself to be upon يقين (Yaqeen). You have to die upon Certainty. This religion is not like I've heard some people speaking, saying, you know what, this is probability. No, it's not probability. Allah in the Quran does not say probability, this is probably True. Allah says this is Yaqeen. YAQEEN IS ABSOLUTE CERTAINTY. So you have to be upon absolute certainty this is from God.", "And now your children, your family members, living in a non-Muslim land, they'd encounter extreme number of doubts from people from every direction, from every ideology, whether that be Christianity, whether that be liberalism, whatever \"isms\" that are available today. And for them to reject these things, they have to already be upon a correct foundation. If they don't have that strong, correct foundation, they're not going to be able to counter these doubts.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Islam Unveiled: Compelling Evidence For The Truthfulness Of Islam | Chicago - USA | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AUFsBco_CF0", ((147, "2:27–3:14"), (196, "3:16–3:53"), (241, "4:01–4:25"), (269, "4:29–4:53"),), id: 3243)
