#passage(("Something you need to understand is that people who speak the Truth are always being fought throughout history. You look at The Prophets of God, you look at the best people, people who'd done well. You talk about Malcolm X a lot; you can see how his life was, how much fighting he had to do. So, do not expect people to be welcoming you when you speak about the Truth. I think it's something that you need to internalise: that people are not going to like you if you speak about the Truth. And my advice, honestly, is that you understand that most people are robotic. They're essentially brainwashed by what they see around them.", "I'm on YouTube, for example, but I have to be very careful with the phrasing when I talk about certain issues. I do it in a smart way. This is the thing. So, I've got three or four videos. One of them actually was removed by YouTube, but I know the reason it was removed. But I think first, I've built a platform, and I've been speaking in a specific way that did not give me a negative persona in the YouTube Community, where YouTube is targeting me or looking at everything, what I say, or what I don't say. And I'm very careful when I talk about \"ABC Gang\", the gays, this and that. Islamically, we don't agree with these specific practices. I do speak about them. If you check my channel, you see I speak about people who are \"ABC Gang\" communities: I spoke with lesbians, transgenders, I spoke with everyone. I spoke with a Zionist IDF Soldier who accepted Islam, which was a bit surprising even for me! That video went so viral that even in the Arab world, my parents, people around me sent me pictures: \"You're on Al Jazeera!\"", "But that person, he came and he was very angry. Talking about Da'wah, and how Da'wah is done: if I were to give him the same energy from the beginning, this would have been a shouting match between me and him. He's already had trauma, he's already had issues. So, if you give him the same energy, it would have been a disaster. Of course, I started the video by speaking about facts, and how the Zionists took over Palestine, how they came from 1917, all of these things, which is history, which is very important, which most people don't know.", "So what I want to say to you is this: you have to be very careful in your way. You're speaking the Truth, but you have to be careful in the way that you speak the Truth. You have to make it in a way which most of these people, that you called Bots, these Bots are receptive to. They're not repelled by it, they're more receptive to it. So your way has to be very intelligent, very smart. Your demeanour, these types of things, I think it's very important. And this is one of the things that the \"Red Pill\" community overlooks: \"No! it's facts, just say it's facts.\" That's not the case; that's not how human beings function. We are humans, and we've got intellect, and we've got emotions. OK, yeah, men are more on the rational side, but they also got emotions, and they also react towards things, if they shock them in a specific way. You try to tailor it in a way in which you will be more suitable for these types of audiences.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Muslim Lantern Gets Sneak∅ To Rethink His Views! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ocg_ABofNVU", ((420, "7:00–7:22"), (455, "7:35–8:54"), (534, "8:54–9:24"), (564, "9:24–10:22"),), id: 3261)
// U ML046:332-387 | The Muslim Lantern | 4
#passage(("I'm not a scholar. But it's not only me; there's many other brothers who are Muslims, and they all have teams, and they're all helping Muslims, and they're inviting them to Islam, bringing them closer to Allah. And alhamdulillah (Praise is due to God), people are having magnificent experiences. I know people who do Da'wah with me who accepted Islam on our table, and they do Da'wa with us. Some of them are writing books about Islam.", "One person treated you badly, and we condemn that if it's true! If it's true, Islam is very clear on being welcoming to other people (anNahl16:125). The word دعوة (Da'wa), which you hear a lot, means INVITATION, actually. If I invite people, I'm supposed to invite people with good mannerisms. I'm not supposed to invite people with evil and anger and stuff like that. It's not the purpose. The purpose is to invite people with a good attitude and good mannerisms. Allah explicitly tells us in the Quran (alAnkabut29:46) (And do not argue with the People of the Book except with that which is best). So this is a clear command in Islam. (Except those who transgress among them), of course: except the evil people, of course, you're allowed to defend yourself. But generally, you're supposed to be welcoming. You're supposed to be good, you're supposed to help people, invite them to Islam, be good to them, be kind to them. There's nothing for you to be proud about.", "Allah, in the Quran (anNisa4:94), spoke to the Companions of the Prophet Muhammadﷺ ('alayhi ssalatu wa sSalam: peace and blessing be upon him), and He told them, (Do not say to the person who gives you Salam or says I'm a believer that you're not a believer). That's a verse in the Quran, where Allah, addressing the Companions, which are supposed to be the best of the people after the Prophet, He's telling them: don't behave that way with someone who says to you \"I'm a believer\"; don't tell him \"you're not a believer\". And then Allah reminds them, He says كَذَٰلِكَ كُنتُم مِّن قَبْلُ (This is how you were before). You were disbelievers before, and you accepted Islam. Then Allah bestowed upon you the blessing of accepting Islam. So, you have to be humble with everyone. Someone comes to you and says to you, I want to be a Muslim, or I'm a Muslim: of course, why not? You got be good to them. Allah says, (call to the way of your Lord with wisdom and good speech) (anNahl16:125). That's what we believe.", "Now, there is bad people everywhere, in every faith, in every tradition, in every ideology. Nobody is going to say every Muslim is perfect. It doesn't exist in any planet, in any religion. There's bad apples and good apples everywhere. But I wouldn't go and say I left something just because I had a bad experience with someone. I have, let's say tens, if not hundreds, of bad experiences with Christians, but I still speak to them! They insult me, they curse, they do all of these things, I still talk to them. I still want good for them. I still invite them to the Truth. That doesn't change anything, that somebody is behaving badly or behaving negatively.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian 'Ex-Muzlim\" Claims He Left Islam Because Of The Behaviour Of Muslims! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oVEbItwZILs", ((793, "13:13–13:35"), (824, "13:44–14:41"), (886, "14:46–15:28"), (930, "15:30–16:08"),), id: 3262)
