#passage(("We apply what we call empathy. Empathy is when we put ourselves in the shoes of others, and that is how I look at the people around me. This is me personally, and this is what Islam teaches you to do: that you have been blessed. God has blessed you by giving you guidance on the Truth of how to behave and how to live your life. Someone else, Allah did not give him that blessing. Maybe he was born into a family where he never encountered the Truth. Maybe his life and his situation were completely different. So his life led him to what he was doing. So rather than you beating him up, maybe it's not his fault. Rather than attacking him, why don't you tell him what is the Truth, what is right? And maybe God will place guidance and hope in his heart, love in his heart, and then he will stop what he's doing, and he will change what he's doing! So that's what we try to do.", "People hear a lot of bad things about us online, and in the media, where they hear a lot of bad things about Muslims. We're here to show the people that what you're hearing is not true, and we are here to present our Faith, to show you what our faith says, not our opinions, but what the Scripture really says, what Allah says and what the Prophet says.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “A Christian Testimony About Islam Part 1! Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qLF3sGWkBek", ((1687, "28:07–28:54"), (1736, "28:56–29:08"),), id: 3263)
