#passage(("We have to look at the person giving the da'wah. Are you qualified to give the dawah or not is the first question that we need to ask. Because dawah can be given in different ways: can be given with your behaviour, Akhlaq (character) as a Muslim, giving your neighbor a gift, being nice to them, helping them, removing obstacles from the road, or doing these things that when people see you, it becomes a source of dawah. As you see many, many people accepting Islam because of the behaviour they see of the Muslims. They mention, oh, I've seen them, how they behave; they're good, they're nice, they're strict upon what they believe, they do good things. This is dawah within itself.", "And other forms of dawah is direct dawah, just directly speak to the person. So if you want to do direct dawah, where you directly speak to the person, then we see if you're qualified, meaning you have the foundation, the fundamentals of the Faith, understanding the أصول, the foundational principles in this religion, and that whatever you say, you speak what you know, and you leave that which you do not know. That's the first thing.", "Now, many people who don't have these skills, how do we do dawah to our people around us? Very simple. Purchase a copy of the Quran and give it to them. There's nothing easier than this. Purchase a copy of the Quran, give it to your neighbour, give it to the co-worker, give it to your friend, and say to them, if you have any questions later, you can ask me. They bring questions, say to them, I'll come back to you with the answer. Anyone is able to do this. There isn't someone who is not able to do this. Say, that's a great question. If you don't know the answer, if it's not as simple as how many prayers do you pray a day, if it's something more difficult, go to someone of knowledge, get the information, get the answers, and come back and give them the answers. But giving them the Quran is a huge step along the way. And your behaviour and manners with them is a huge step along the way.", "I heard that there are not many dawah tables here; we need to change this. If you have this information, you just go to the dawah table and just present it. You just sit at the dawah table and give free Quran. It's enough to establish the Truth with these people, without argumentation, without many back and forth, just presenting this information, leading them to people of knowledge. If they have questions you don't know, you go seek the answers. We need to establish this here. Tens of people are sitting here. Why are we not able to go and set up a dawah stall? And there are some brothers who are doing it. Why are we not doing more? Why are we not doing it in more locations, different locations? It's to be done.", "If you don't feel like you're a person of knowledge, set up the stall. Seek knowledge every day, as it's an obligation of every Muslim, and give the Quran to the people, and you have done your effort. InshaAllah, we need to do that. Put that intention. And know this is for your goodness, for your آخرة (Akhira: Hereafter) before it is for anyone else.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Islam Unveiled: Compelling Evidence For The Truthfulness Of Islam | Chicago - USA | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AUFsBco_CF0", ((4133, "1:08:53–1:09:26"), (4168, "1:09:28–1:09:49"), (4191, "1:09:51–1:10:35"), (4243, "1:10:43–1:11:54"), (4318, "1:11:58–1:12:36"),), id: 3271)
