#passage(("A lot of people struggle with that. Even Muslims struggle with that, whether you're Muslim or non-Muslim. Because we as Muslims would have parents that would do certain things that were wrong, and it's difficult for you to tell them.", "Generally speaking, there are certain people that certain methods work with them, and there are certain people where only guidance is from God. So for instance, Prophet Muhammadﷺ was better than any of us in conveying the Message, but his uncle, for instance: he was conveying the Message to him. He was doing it. But then he died rejecting it. And then Allahﷻ revealed to him that (You do not guide the ones you choose, Allah is The One Who chooses to guide) [alQasas28:56]. It's in the heart. The hearts are in the Hands of God. I can try my best, but Allah gives us examples of the uncles of the Prophetﷺ, etc. not being believers, being among the enemies his whole life. So you can understand that guidance is from God, from Allahﷻ. And this life is a test.", "But also a very important thing is this: you could bring someone other than yourself. Maybe someone else would respect, would listen to, more than you. You can bring someone that they don't know. Maybe they would be willing to have a discussion with them more than they would with their own son. So with their own son, they'd be like, you know what, yesterday I was teaching you; now you want to tell me what I should believe? But bringing someone else who they don't know, or someone who's respectful in community, etc., someone like that, who knows how to give the Message, can be the best way. You can invite them to a mosque in which there is someone who's making an open day and making these events, speaking about Islam, so they can listen. Not even have a conversation, but listen. You can give them videos to listen to. You can give them different ways as much as you can, indirect ways, or bringing someone else other than you that conveys the Message to them, if you feel, when