#passage(("We have our own concept. So, for me, you can have your concept, and I can critique your concept rationally, you can critique my concept rationally. That's why I’m saying you can. I’m giving you the ground. I'm saying if you want to do it, you can, because I'm not sensitive about my religion. All I care about is a few things. First, that you're a respectful person. You engage with me, you have a dialogue, like we're trying to have a dialogue. We don't interrupt each other. I'll present my evidence and reasoning, you'll present your evidence and reasoning, and, hopefully, we're seeking the Truth. But when it comes to [tit for tat] and scoring points, this is not my way.", "And I don't get offended by that at all, not even.. zero! Can I tell you the difference? I'm saying try and find your holes. It's OK! For us it's not a problem. My problem is not trying to find the holes; my problem is being rude, is to curse the prophet, trying to talk about his character. Muslims don't do that. Even in the park, Muslims don't do that! I believe that it should be about interaction. It should be that you're presenting something, I’m presenting something. We're rational human beings, respectful people and individuals who should not be cursing and attacking individuals, especially the people that other people hold to be holy individuals and have respect for. I cannot come and start insulting Mary just to get a reaction out of them.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Preacher Speaks The Truth! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qcg1xskpwHI", ((490, "8:10–8:40"), (561, "9:21–11:03"),), id: 3325)
