#passage(("Something really strange happened to me today. I went off to one of those little supermarkets – not even supermarket, they just sell sweets and chips. And while I was there, a guy came in and he was like, \"Hey, Patrick, Patrick.\" He comes up to me. He chases me around. And he's like, \"Oh, you look like my friend Patrick. My bad.\" And then it ended with him saying, \"Where are you from?\" I said, \"From the Middle East.\" And he kind of apologized about the Middle East. It was the strangest thing. And he started talking about a list of countries that were supposed to be invaded. So I'm thinking he's going to try to mug me. And then I started noticing some things about him. He's scratching his hands furiously, and he had this huge blood stain on his ear.", "Here's what shocks me. He's like, \"We're all kind of similar, is just you believe in Allah and we believe in Jesus.\" And I realized this guy is here to do da'wah to me. Actually walked into the convenience store to do da'wah to me, and started calling out Patrick, Patrick. Subhanallah. And his evidence for Christianity, not really too much. He had visions, and Jesus appeared to him in the washroom, and he saw blood everywhere. And then he wanted to exchange numbers. I took his number; you got to be nice. And the whole time I'm thinking there's nothing I can say to this guy; I can't do that with a guy while he's in this condition.", "But now here's a thing: I so appreciate that he actually went out of his way to do [da'wah] to me. I really appreciate it, in his state, without evidence for whatever he's upon. Of course you need to have some [ilm] to do [da'wah], without a doubt, but even with a lack of [ilm], he just wanted to share that message with me. So I'm hoping we can have that same zeal as well.",), "Farid Responds, “Unexpected Exchange in South Carolina”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BCC3JC1oUrk", ((10, "0:10–2:31"), (203, "3:23–4:21"), (263, "4:23–4:54"),), id: 3329)

