#passage(("Now, the nice thing about the internet is that we have access to a lot of information, not just information in general, but refutation information. So often, if you are troubled by a specific question, all you got to do is google it, and first couple of results, I'm sure you're gonna find a satisfying answer. Of course, sometimes you're going to face information that's against Islam, sometimes rebuttals to the information that you find in the first two results. But there's something that you have to keep in mind when that occurs: you have to return to the original article, the original refutation, in order to see if the information was properly refuted. Believe it or not, they will actually put up responses to Islamic refutations just because they feel the pressure, and when you look into their work, you will find no substance whatsoever. So once again, what I strongly recommend is: after seeing a counter refutation, return to the refutation itself and see if the points were properly addressed.",), "Farid Responds, “Refutations 101 [Crash Course]”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CgfiwsD4Sns", ((1968, "32:48–33:57"),), id: 3348)
