#passage(("I'm kind of new to defending Islam, relatively speaking; [I've] been doing it for 5 years. Before that I was mainly involved in Sunni [Shia] matters, and I saw an evolution within myself. I dropped a lot of the arguments that I used to use. I only stick with arguments I consider to be very compelling, nothing that could be turned around against me. I'm not going to be throwing stones from within a glass house. Now, unfortunately, many Christians lack this self-reflection, and they attempt to refute Islam using everything in the kitchen sink, and due to this, when they use these arguments, they look bad, they look ridiculous. They seem to believe that every argument against Islam is a good one: Islam is false, and therefore every argument against Islam is a good one.",), "Farid Responds, “The Dumbest Argument against Islam EVER!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WhcJLgflN-E", ((75, "1:15–2:00"),), id: 3350)
