#passage(("Why did they leave their culture and decide to adopt the faith of Islam? So why Islam? If they have a problem with Catholicism, they can move to anything else. Why specifically Islam? Judaism, Hinduism, Buddhism, so many -isms today.", "Islam is rational. It makes sense. Islam will fit your mind. We say as Muslims, something that is within every human, it's called the فطرة Fitrah. فطرة is an innate disposition that God created us with. So it's an innate disposition that every human being has. So when things pop in your mind, or that makes sense, we say that فطرة is awakening (has been covered by your community or society and people around you).", "So that's why those Polish women, when they came across Islamic teachings and they saw how Islam honors women, while the media says the opposite, they actually started searching, reading what the Quran says, and realized that Islam honors women, that Islam fits with the innate thing, that within the heart makes sense to them as a peaceful religion. And it is a community religion. There's a brotherhood and sisterhood, and there are actual concerns about people: something happens to them, you know your neighbors, you know the people around you, you know people in the mosque. [Mosques] are full, they're not empty. So many beautiful things about Islam that we can speak about.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Polish Student Amazed By Islamic Teachings! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pf1BQGnAXZc", ((347, "5:47–6:19"), (396, "6:36–7:32"), (457, "7:37–8:06"),), id: 3365)
