// U ML402:509-532 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("Do you know what a Muslim is? A Muslim is someone who believes there is a Creator. That Creator is not a man or a woman. The Creator created everything: All-Powerful, created the world, is Merciful, is Wise. And He sends Messengers like Jesus, Moses, Noah, Abraham, and these people. They bring revelation from God. And Prophet Muhammadﷺ is the last Messenger who's sent to us, and he brought the Quran for us as a Messenger. If someone believes in these two basic things, then that person believes what a Muslim believes.", "But if you testify, then you officially become a Muslim. You officially enter the faith of Islam. And then there are practices that you take step by step. Because a lot of people, they think: OK, I'm going to tell my family, I'm going to do this, I'm going to do that. We usually say: keep it for yourself in the beginning. Become Muslim, read the Quran, think about things step by step.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Truth About Philosophy! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xoYG4Qi-lx4", ((1222, "20:22–20:51"), (1266, "21:06–21:18"),), id: 3370)
