#passage(("The shahada is how you become Muslim. Shahada is to testify that you believe there's only one God worthy of worship, and you believe that Prophet Muhammad is his messenger. When you say that, you say in Arabic and English, then you enter into Islam. And that testimony of Faith, the shahada, is how you enter Paradise, if you die with that belief. You do your best, you practice as much as you can. It's difficult; do as much as you can.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Surprises A French Man Looking For Answers! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=piz443ivKUc", ((482, "8:02–8:26"),), id: 3371)
// U ML314:732-752 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("It's just on the person who did not do it correctly, did not explain to you what it means to take the Shahada: that you actually become a Muslim and you leave associated partners of God. You actually try to now worship God and follow the commands of God in the Quran. Some people do it, unfortunately, for themselves, because they know they would be rewarded for leading people to good. It's about the people actually sincerely accepting that thing and sincerely wanting to follow it.", "You cannot speak about the future that we're living in today without being a Messenger of God; prophecies are from Prophets only.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Does Jesus Possess The Attributes of God?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2Jp6DQffnZg", ((2203, "36:43–37:18"), (2263, "37:43"),), id: 3372)
// U ML043:447-478 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("Accepting Islam is a very simple process. You can do it right now, you can do it when you feel like it; there's no pressure. The thing about Islam is the TRUTH, so we don't need to go and force anybody to accept it. We welcome people, we send invitations, friendly invitations to people: here's the Truth and here's why it's the Truth, and we welcome you to accept Islam. All you have to do is to testify there's nothing worthy of worship except Allah, the same God of Jesus, and to testify that Prophet Muhammad is His Prophet and Messenger. That's it! Once you make that testimony, you become a Muslim.", "What matters is that we accept the Truth. If I still have a question, let me investigate that question. But what matters in the end is: I don't look for what benefits me, I look for what is True, and I follow that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Questions A Muslim On The Return Of Jesus Then This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EepfuZMN91I", ((1236, "20:36–21:13"), (1292, "21:32–21:42"),), id: 3373)
// U ML212:351-392 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("Sometimes we're used to certain things, and we do them out of habit. Being around a good company, you'll find these people reminding you not to say this; then gradually that habit will go away, that bad habit will go away. It's also the people you're around. It's very important.", "EVERYONE HAS AN INVITATION TO ISLAM. It's open for everyone. If you ever want to become Muslim, you're welcome. If you've got questions, you're also welcome to ask these questions, if you think something is keeping you away. If Islam makes sense to you, reading it makes sense to you, the beliefs of Islam make sense to you, believe in it; then you're there from a belief perspective. But then taking the step and testifying to what you believe, and then step by step trying to learn how to pray, how to connect with God, to give God His right, not to disobey Him anymore, to be around good company.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sincere Christian Speaks The Truth About Christianity! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JhnP-6KOjWY", ((1128, "18:48–19:06"), (1152, "19:12–19:44"),), id: 3374)
// U ML180:132-199 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("If you agree that Prophet Muhammad is a messenger of God, and you look at Jesus as a messenger of God, and you believe in one God only worthy of worship, what's the difference between you and me? If this is the case, then there is no difference: what you believe is what we believe; then you have Muslim beliefs. Meaning, if you go to the church and say what I just told you and what you believe, they'll kick you out: \"You're not a Christian.\" If you go to any other religion on Earth, they would say: you believe what Muslims believe, you don't believe what we believe. So what you believe is specific to one religion, which is Islam.", "We don't say only Prophet Muhammad, because in Islam, if you don't believe in any of the other Messengers, you're a disbeliever; you have to believe in all of them. Allah says in the Quran explicitly that the messenger has believed in that which was revealed to him from his Lord, and so have the Believers: everyone has believed in Allah and his Messengers, all of the messengers, saying: we make no distinction between the messengers. So I cannot believe in Moses and then leave Jesus. I have to believe in all of them. So if a Muslim says: \"I'm a Muslim, I believe in Prophet Muhammad, I don't believe Jesus existed\", you're [a disbeliever], you're not a Muslim; it doesn't matter what you say. If he says \"I don't believe in Moses\", it's the same thing. You have to believe in all of them.", "The person says they believe that there's only one God worthy of worship, Allah. Allah is the name of God, and that God is not like you and me: not a man, is not a woman, doesn't have children and grandparents. He's not like the creation; he's powerful, independent, he's just uniquely one. That's what Allah means. So you say: I believe nothing is worthy of worship except Allah. You don't worship animals, you don't worship humans, you don't worship trees; worship Allah. And you believe that Prophet Muhammad is his messenger and servant. If someone says that, call it the [shahada]; then they enter into the fold of Islam.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sincere Lady About To Accept Islam But This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V2bQy_K4u5g", ((248, "4:08–4:42"), (304, "5:04–5:41"), (341, "5:41–6:16"),), id: 3375)
// U ML290:520-551 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("I'm happy for you becoming Muslim anytime. But the thing is, I want you to do it from yourself, from your decision, from when you want to make it yourself. You can read the Quran if you want; you can do it if you want, as long as you believe in what it teaches, meaning that you believe that there's a Creator that created everything, is not a man or a woman, is not a picture or Idol. It is beyond the comprehension of the human beings, the Creator. When it comes to His full Glory, you cannot really understand that. And we know some of His attributes: that He's Merciful, Caring, Loving and Powerful and Just, and all of these different attributes, and Knowing. And you believe that He sends Prophets and Messengers to connect people with Him, and that the Quran is a Revelation coming from the Creator through the Prophet and the Messenger, Prophet Muhammad, or Revelation coming from God through any other Prophet or Messenger in the past that was sent.", "So if you believe these things, essentially you're there from a knowledge perspective. You're ready to become a Muslim from a knowledge perspective. Now, willingness to do it, that will obviously come back to you. I'll let you read the Quran: get a copy of Sahih International.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “American Lady Learns The Truth About Palestine! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WKGqYmu6paw", ((1709, "28:29–29:32"), (1775, "29:35–29:53"),), id: 3376)
