#passage(("Prophet Muhammad was a Messenger of God, and if he said he's the last one, then he was the last one.", "Then what we do is, once you accept Islam, I'll connect you with our team. We have a sister's team. What they will do, they will help you with the gradual steps. Everything is baby steps. Nobody just accepts and then does everything! No, you take your time. You start understanding what is the obligations that God has from you, but step by step: you start first learning about Allah, learning how to pray before anything else.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Baha'i Lady Questions Muslim On The Last Prophet! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5_h1_yrAXLg", ((1439, "23:59–24:01"), (1458, "24:18–24:37"),), id: 3377)
// U ML212:285-305 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("Prophet Muhammadﷺ, he was a Messenger from God. He's saying: follow these principles that come from God, the same principles that God gave to Jesus, that God gave to Moses, that God gave to Abraham: to worship One God Alone, to not associate partners with Him, to know that this life is a test, to do that which is morally good, and avoid that which is evil. These teachings are the teachings that Prophet Muhammadﷺ came with.", "So if you accept that he's a Messenger of God, like Moses was, like Abraham was, like Noah was, like Jesus was, like all of these Messengers that were sent from God (their job was to connect people with the Creator, to tell them about God and to give them that Revelation, the Message of God to them, and then to tell them to abide by and follow, and be examples themselves), if you believe that, then you believe what a Muslim believes.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sincere Christian Speaks The Truth About Christianity! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JhnP-6KOjWY", ((844, "14:04–14:26"), (869, "14:29–14:53"),), id: 3378)
// U ML279:358-390 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("So what about Prophet Muhammadﷺ then? If you look at his teachings, he taught people to believe in Jesus, that Mary was a pure woman that had Jesus without male intervention, without a father; that teaches you about Moses, and he was a pure Prophet of God. And all the Prophets of God were pure people trying their best. When we say pure, we don't mean they're perfect, but they don't commit these major, hideous acts. This is what Muslims believe about those Prophets and Messengers.", "Also, the Quran is a Message from God that affirms that there was a Prophet who got Revelation from God called Jesus. That Revelation is not preserved anymore. And that Moses got a revelation from God, but that is not preserved anymore. And that's what history shows. Anyone who does any actual investigation about Manuscripts will realise there's no such thing from the time of Jesus, there's no such thing from the time of Moses, and whatever we have is from unknown people.", "So if you believe in these basic principles, that Prophet Muhammadﷺ is the Messenger of God and the Quran is from God, essentially you believe in the minimum things for a person to become a Muslim.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Highlights The Inconsistency Of The Bible! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KcRdd8LsvKE", ((1144, "19:04–19:48"), (1194, "19:54–20:12"), (1215, "20:15–20:21"),), id: 3379)
// U ML227:587-615 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("There are many ways you could say the Shahada that are found in the Quran and Hadith. You could even say at the end of the Shahada that Jesus is the Messenger of God as well, if someone was coming from a Christian background, to affirm that he no longer believes that he's God, for example. So there is صِيَغ. Siyagh is the way to say something. There's many Siagh, many ways of saying the Shahada that are authentically attributed and transmitted to us. So there's many ways you could say it, and it's up to your choice. Sometimes I might say this one, sometimes I might say that one, whichever happens at the time. Sometimes ones are shorter, sometimes ones are a bit longer, but they all mean the same thing: either to say the Prophet Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, or to add that he's also the Servant and Messenger. But all of them are reliable and accepted.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Compares Islam And Christianity! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Igzqbqr2Pew", ((2130, "35:30–36:18"),), id: 3380)
// U ML200:147-180 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("There is something called \"the Shahada\". The Shahada is a Testimony of Faith. And what it renews is that any sins that you ever did in your life: if you do the Shahada, you say that testimony of faith and become Muslim and practise, then Allah forgives all your previous sins. So you have a new, clean, clear slate that is free of any sins, if you accept Islam and start practising Islam into your life. And it's also recommended that you take a full shower, so you internally cleanse and also externally cleanse after you say that Testimony of Faith.", "And that testimony of faith is to testify: 1- There's nothing worthy of worship except Allah: ALLAH IS THE ONLY GOD. 2- And that Prophet Muhammad (Peace and blessings of God be upon him) is His Messenger and Servant: His Prophet that has been sent by Him to you and to all mankind and all humanity. So that is what we have in Islam. We use the term Shahada and the term \"Acceptance of Faith\".",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Asks Muslim A Very Difficult Question! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_EOVzP3AwkE", ((423, "7:03–7:29"), (454, "7:34–7:53"),), id: 3381)
// U ML180:523-559 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("You believe what you need to believe to be a Muslim. What's important now is the Practical aspects of your life. And it's very important to know that right now, if you die from a Muslim belief, you've not died upon the truth. So it's not enough for someone to just say \"I believe in these things\": unless someone takes a shahada, testimony of faith, and practices Islam in his life, if he dies, we believe that person will be punished; the person doesn't go to paradise, because you've never testified what you truly need to testify towards God, and you never implemented in your life. Because anyone can say: oh, I do this, I do that, but they're not really living in accordance to what God has commanded them to live by. So if you have that belief, then I think it's very important for you to understand the need and necessity for you to actually take it into practical steps, in application in your life.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sincere Lady About To Accept Islam But This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V2bQy_K4u5g", ((1031, "17:11–17:57"),), id: 3382)
