#passage(("The thing about her is: what she explained is her worry of saying \"I'm a Muslim\", of how people are going to perceive it. Deep down, it seems she consider herself a Muslim, but it's about publicly to declare it: \"Oh guys, look, I am a Muslim.\" Then she met the bad friends, and they were like: \"Why you fasting?\" This and that. As Allah tells us, there are shayatin of humans. Shaitan is not only jinn. It's also humans that can push you away from religion. It can push you away from God, or that can call you to evil. That's why you cannot be around people like that. Those are not your friends. What does the word friend mean? Someone who wants good for you. Can be your friend who is pushing you away from that which is good for you? No.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “New Convert Questions Muslim On Lack Of Connection With God In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pwUuzBBM4o8", ((1465, "24:25–25:12"),), id: 3383)
