#passage(("I just remembered something funny. It was a story about someone who wanted to get divorced from his wife, but he was Christian. So he had no option except to accept Islam to then get divorced from his wife! \"I'm Muslim now, and then I'm going to divorce you!\" It was a funny story that I read before. That teaching in Christianity does not make any sense anyways.", "Truth can sometimes be convenient. So if the Truth is convenient, there's no problem in choosing to follow the Truth because it's convenient. But the problem is when you do something wrong because it's convenient. Allah is not trying to make things difficult for us. So if Allah is making something easy for you, and someone decides to accept because it's made easier for them, then that makes sense. But for someone to accept Islam, you have to believe in the teachings of Islam, or they're not Muslims. So if they say \"I accept Islam so that I can divorce my wife\", but they don't believe in Allah or Prophet Muhammad, they're not Muslim. Because how you enter Islam is that you have to believe in Allah and Prophet Muhammad as His Messenger. This is the \"Shahada\". If you don't believe in that and testify to it, you cannot be a Muslim: that you accept His Messenger to be the Prophet Muhammad, and you follow him in that which he has commanded you to do.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Curious Lady Grills Muslim With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2EcJiOmZI44", ((1572, "26:12–26:35"), (1628, "27:08–28:00"),), id: 3384)

