#passage(("So I'm saying now rationally, why would you not then? Because you can see the wisdom in Islam. You can see the truth. You can see the evidences. You can see the rationality behind. Then the rational discourse to do is to know: okay, my ancestors told me something. Allah even tells us that in the Quran: the pagan Arabs at the time of the prophet used to worship idols. Allah says in the Quran just because your ancestors did something or they teach you something doesn't mean they're right. What if they were wrong? What if they were misguided? You need to use your rationality and you apply an evidence-based criteria to come to the conclusion of what is the truth.", "That is how you arrive to this conclusion that Islam is the truth. Then I would say the rational decision of you to do right now is to accept Islam, is to move a step forward and say: okay, this makes sense to me, that is from God; let me follow it and let me practice it in my life. Now other religions, you want to look at them, you can look at them, but trust me, the more you look at them the more you'll know that's not from God, because they will not make sense, they will not be accurate. They will be for your harm rather than for your benefit. So why not take that step and become a Muslim?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Rational Thinker Asks A Muslim Thought-Provoking Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=myrg5IOTPBI", ((1254, "20:54–21:30"), (1292, "21:32–22:06"),), id: 3389)
