#passage(("For you the important thing is that you become a Muslim, and not to worry too much about these Shias, Ahmadis, and to confuse yourself. The important thing is that you start with the first few steps, which is that you know there's a Creator, God's existence. After that, you move to: Islam is the Truth, because you know about the evidences of Islam. [For] example, the Quran talks about biological life is all from water, talks about the universe expanding, talks about biological life, and how the baby literally develops in the womb. Professor Keith Moore, who's a Christian, he's not Muslim, but he said the information here can only come from God. An Arab bedouin 1400 years ago without microscopes cannot tell you how the baby develops in the mother's womb. So this information makes assurance this has to be from God! And if it is from God, then we need to follow it! So I'm telling you, you should be following it.", "If you want to bring maybe a Shia next time with you, I can talk to him, no problem. Bring anyone from any tradition. Because I want to show you that it's not just what I'm saying, but even if they were here they wouldn't be able to answer the questions I was giving you. Focus on reading the Quran for now, and once you feel you're ready come back and you can accept Islam.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Questioned On Sectarianism In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MnwLenfsZWA", ((1002, "16:42–17:36"), (1089, "18:09–18:27"),), id: 3394)
