#passage(("Why not take that step then? If the Quran makes sense to you, and you've read it. I can tell you tons of Hadiths; I'm sure you will say this is the most wise thing you could ever hear. The Prophet's teachings and Narrations: \"None of you becomes a believer until you love for your brother what you love for yourself.\" Prophet said: \"You're not a believer if your neighbour sleeps hungry and you're full.\" The Prophet mentions that \"from the perfection of your faith, that you leave that which is not of your business.\" The Prophet talks about richness and he says: \"true richness is the richness of the heart, not money.\"", "The Prophet gives these examples and parables to his Companions, where he says: \"Do you know who's the bankrupt person?\" And they say: \"the bankrupt person is the one who doesn't have money.\" He says to them: \"No, the bankrupt person is the one who prays, and gives charity\" –How is he bankrupt?– \"He gives charity, prays,\" and does all of that, \"but he goes and curses this person, and insults that person.\" Which we have so many people like this: they pray and do the rights of God, BUT they leave the rights of humans!", "So if you look at the Narrations, you can see the wisdom of the Prophet, which is a Revelation from God in the end! Allah says: (he doesn't speak of his own, it's only Revelation being given) (anNajm53:3-4) وَمَا یَنطِقُ عَنِ ٱلۡهَوَىٰۤ () إِنۡ هُوَ إِلَّا وَحۡیࣱ یُوحَىٰ This is the truth! So, I would encourage you to take this step. Of course, you can take your time if you want; this is just a suggestion and an invitation, a friendly invitation. Imagine me inviting you to my wedding or something: it's a friendly invitation, and it's up to you to act upon it or not.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Romanian Christian Grills Muslim With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RCeSQlWHPxI", ((1566, "26:06–26:39"), (1605, "26:45–27:04"), (1629, "27:09–27:37"),), id: 3398)
