#passage(("If you grew up all your life thinking Santa Claus comes in from your chimney, and then someone tells you, \"you know what? That's just a fairytale!\" You just realise it's a false belief. You don't believe it anymore. Even if I believed in something my entire existence and my entire life, once I realise and see objective evidence that this is wrong, I need to stop believing it. Now, not to do that is by definition called \"Delusion\". Delusion is to believe something opposite to the objective reality and evidences being against it. So you see the objective facts and reality and you believe the opposite. We cannot be delusional. We cannot live in delusion just because someone taught us something.", "Allah says in the Quran about the pagan Arabs: \"they said, this is what we found our forefathers upon\" (alBaqara2:170). Allah said, \"What if your forefathers were not guided?\" \"What if they were ignorant?\" \"What if they didn't know?\" Aren't there many things that your parents told you that were not accurate? Many things that my parents told me that were not accurate, and then when you grow up you realise, \"OK, that was not true.\" A part of growing up, but mentally, is to abandon false ideologies and accept the guidance that comes to you from God. You have to be an honest person. That's what sincerity is. Sincerity is to accept the Truth when the Truth comes to you.", "I'll give you another hypothetical example. Let's say your whole life you've been adopted. You don't know you're adopted. You believe you're from your parents, 100%. But let's say you are adopted, and then your parents come to you, and they give you a DNA test: are you still going to believe you're the biological son? But you believed it your whole life! Which part of Islam being the Truth, or what I've given you, that is not black and white? I think it's more black and white, because the DNA test can be forged and my parents could have other alternatives. But with Islam, I'm more sure that it is true than the DNA test.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Refuses To Accept Rational Evidences For Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KFpgNsX6nJ4", ((1121, "18:41–19:21"), (1164, "19:24–19:59"), (1207, "20:07–20:42"),), id: 3417)
