// U ML394:382-417 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("We don't have time. We don't know. Today, I'm here; tomorrow I'm not here. You go to the graves: very young people, 15, 16, 17. People are in the grave! Death does not have favourites. It's not going to tell: OK, until you become 60, I'll give you that time. We have this hope, false hope in our mind: when I get 60, I'm gonna die. How do you know? We don't know. We can die any day. We can cross the street any day. And if God created us here to test us, then we are failing the test if we don't accept the Truth before we die.", "So, I invite you both to Islam. I invite you both to accept Islam, so you get a Reward, so you do not be of those people who don't get a reward, who get punished.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Priests Force Their Beliefs?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SU-3La7AfR4", ((837, "13:57–14:22"), (870, "14:30–14:36"),), id: 3424)
// U ML189:319-371 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("God tells us that this life is the test that we're in, and there isn't another life: the other life is the eternal life. So in that life you cannot choose to believe in this and that; it is accountability. If this life is a test, it's like you have a piece of paper. I took it from you. Now imagine you go to the Professor: \"Can you give me the paper?\" \"Sorry, time is over. Here is your degree; this is what you did.\" This life is like that. Think about it. We are in a limited time. The answers is whether we'll obey, listen to what God taught us to do good, or we will do wrong. And once we die, that piece of paper is taken.", "Because Allah says in the Quran people will wish they can come back, say: give us another chance and we will believe. Allah said: but you were here, I had so many chances, people told you about me, I give you signs; why did you not follow me? I was giving you food, I was providing for you, you're breathing, you're happy, having a nice friend, all of that. So what stopped you then from being thankful? And the only way you can be thankful is to actually obey God. Can I say I'm thankful, but I'm going to ignore everything God has commanded me to do? So don't delay that. Allah tells you to hurry into worshiping God, to hurry into forgiveness of God, and the only way we can ascertain that is by obeying him, by following the commands that came from him.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian and Muslim Debate Who Deserves Heaven! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wBWcO-JMcmU", ((671, "11:11–11:48"), (708, "11:48–12:51"),), id: 3425)
// U ML347:663-697 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("What Satan does is he whispers to you. He puts the ideas in your mind. Let's say you've got clarity, that makes sense; he starts putting ideas in your mind: No no! but you've got this, but you've got that, but this problem is there... You start feeling this heavy burden on your shoulders for no reason. And the fact is, when you rationally think about it, you realize there is no problem. Because if you accept Islam and you encounter something that is completely major that shows you that this is not The Truth, who's gonna stop you from saying: OK, I'm not going to become Muslim anymore? It's just a game that Satan is playing with your mind, trying to delay you, delay you, until you die.", "We don't know! Allah says in the Quran that we are supposed to say to the people who don't believe that you do not know when death comes to you! If I knew when death is coming to me, then everyone will do whatever they want and in the end they will seek repentance: Oh Allah forgive me, I'm coming back to the Truth! So that is what makes this life a test: because you don't know. So, you need to hasten into doing the good deeds. You cannot play games with Allah. If I know that you are my Creator, you're my Lord, you created me, you sent me Prophets and Messengers, I know this message is from you, I've got no excuse to delay, except that I'm doing whatever I want to do.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Challenges Muslim On God Then This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MSk1AiEaXH8", ((2003, "33:23–33:56"), (2050, "34:10–34:40"),), id: 3426)
// U ML397:258-287 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("What we say as Muslims is that Allah chose you today to accept Islam. Why? Allah saw in you sincerity. We don't believe things just happen like this. What we believe is that Allah has destined the things that happen every day. So, you did not just walk by. Allah destined you to come here today. He wanted you to listen in order to hear this information. He tested you to see whether you will accept the Truth or you're not going to accept the Truth.", "So many people, they hear the Truth. \"Does it make sense?\" \"It makes sense.\" \"Do you want to accept?\" \"No!\" \"Why? It makes sense to you, right?\" Because life is more important to them. The worldly things are more important to them: drugs, alcohol, women, all of these issues that they might, in the future, need to leave. They don't want to leave. Or maybe think that: \"I will have to do this, I will have to do that. Just live your life, man.\" But I did not create myself. I did not bring myself here, and I don't control when I die. So, if I do follow your advice and I just live my life and follow anything like this, and then I happen to die, are you going to protect me from the Creator? Are you going to stop the fact, the Truth that this is a reality from God? I can pretend the building doesn't exist. The building does exist. It doesn't matter what I think, because the facts are there. The evidences are there, the Truth is there.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Why Should I Accept Your Religion?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rBgIryv7XPM", ((684, "11:24–11:48"), (712, "11:52–12:40"),), id: 3427)
// U ML394:314-340 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("What you believe, in essence, is what Muslims believe in. What you believe in is what we believe in. So, what is stopping you, really, from becoming a Muslim? 3 of every 4 people who accept Islam are women; 70% of people who accept Islam are women.", "Do you know when you're gonna die? So, do you know that you'll be able to take that step before you die? We say this is a play, a step, of Satan. Satan wants you to die as a disbeliever, because if you die as a disbeliever, you end up in Hellfire, and he wins. We say: if something makes sense to me, if you already believe in what Islam teaches, then why would I delay something that makes sense to me? If you accept Islam today, you will continue to learn. If you don't accept today, you will continue to learn. The difference's that you've guaranteed yourself to go to Paradise if you die.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Priests Force Their Beliefs?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SU-3La7AfR4", ((665, "11:05–11:21"), (705, "11:45–12:12"),), id: 3428)
// U ML403:445-481 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("You're not going to come back. I know. Shaytan will pull you away, and Shaytan will drag you step by step. I know, I have experience. Wallahi, one person, he became Muslim, and he was like you. He used to thank us every day. He said, \"If it weren't for you guys, I would have stayed the way I was. I would not have moved forward.\" Because he was there. You are there. You tell me: I believe this is from Allah, I believe in Prophet Muhammad. Did I tell you about Prophet Muhammad? You already told me you believe. Did I tell you to believe in the Quran? You already told me you believe. So I don't need to tell you anything. You're already there. The first thing you said to me was what? \"I'm going to convert, but not now.\" You're coming ready to do it. I've not done anything here. I'm just reminding you that these things are Shaytan stopping you from moving forward, nothing else.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Emotional Shahada! Brother Accepts Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hvQ9biPlbos", ((901, "15:01–15:59"),), id: 3429)
// U ML243:398-445 | The Muslim Lantern | 4
#passage(("You're welcome to accept Islam if you want to accept Islam right now, or if you're feeling like you want to do it later, it's up to you completely. It's your decision. But once you know something is the Truth, it's important not to delay that, because we could leave this life any day. And then if God says to you: you know this is the Truth, but you didn't accept it, essentially you've got nothing to say! Because you admitted, testified this is the Truth. And you know deep down that this is the Truth.", "Now, when it comes to the family: of course, everyone has struggles. There are a lot of things that you might need to leave, a lot of things that you might need to change. No one can give you sugarcoated things. This is the reality! So you become Muslim, there are bad things in your life that you will need to leave. You're not leaving them for any other reason other than the fact that they're harmful to you. So when Allah says leave them, it's because they are not good for you. There will be struggles, but in the end, people accept. They'll come to accept the fact that OK, this is the Truth.", "And in fact, then it becomes now your job in a way to also tell the people the Truth, because you care about them, the people around you, to explain to them why did you take that decision. Because in the end, it was not: you woke up one day and decided to accept Islam or something! You've done research. You came to the conclusion that this is the Truth based on doing research. And that should be always the answer if someone asks why did you do this: here's the reason, because of one, two, three, four, and that's it.", "There's always backlash in the beginning if people are very religious in a different religion, but always as time goes by, they start understanding a bit more. This is always the case, but there is a struggle in the beginning. And Allah says in the Quran (Al'ankabut29:2) (Do not think you'll say, I believe and you'll not be tested). This is evidence that we believe! Anyone can say, I believe, but when the test comes, then we know the people who believe from those who are not as strong in their faith.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “American Man Changes His Mind After Reading The Quran! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q1fh-dV6Szc", ((1430, "23:50–24:08"), (1452, "24:12–24:39"), (1483, "24:43–25:04"), (1508, "25:08–25:29"),), id: 3430)
