#passage(("Islam affirms Jesus was a prophet of God, and he came to deliver a message to the people; that there was Moses, there was Abraham. Islam doesn't completely reject these things as if they didn't exist. The Quran affirms that there was previous messengers sent, previous revelation.", "I think you're rationally there. I think you should move on and take your step. You watch tons of debates. You've looked for the evidence and you see the truth. You've accepted and admitted that there's no other alternative options. The only thing left for you now is to take that step and become a Muslim in practice. It's the only thing left for you to do.", "I don't get anything from you becoming Muslim, nor does anyone. So you're getting it the wrong way, if you think that people are going to lose something. It's for the benefit of you as a human being. If the people don't truly believe, or I don't truly believe, that this is good for you, there would be no point of me talking to you about it, because there's no one waiting to wire 1 million pounds to me once you become a Muslim. So, in the end, it's for your own benefit, whether you move and [take] that step or not.", "You say that it's one conversation, but it's not true, because you're telling me you've been spending months researching and watching discussions, and you have discussions with other Muslims as well, and you watching videos of Muslims. If you are someone that I just met, because I do meet people a lot on the street, they haven't researched Islam, have no clue, then I'll have a conversation, I invite them to Islam. I don't tell them take your shahada, because the person is the first time hearing about the religion. I'm going just give him the basics. It's like if I tell him just jump into this, it makes no sense. But for you, you've already done plenty of research. You're talking about reading the book with the prophecies already, with references. You're not someone who just had one conversation with me. If you're asking me, I believe you're already there, because once you admit: okay, I agree that there's no way prophet Muhammad cannot be a messenger of God, once you reach a stage, then you're a Muslim.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Puts Islam And Christianity To The Test! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7qT2I7lBW18", ((2734, "45:34–45:47"), (2759, "45:59–46:20"), (2830, "47:10–48:02"), (2882, "48:02–49:11"),), id: 3431)
