#passage(("I couldn't help it but comment on what just happened. You see someone who refers to themselves as a Muslim, Subhan Allah, they see someone who is about to take their step and accept the religion of Islam, and they become the means of preventing them. They become the people who are doing the work of [Shaytan]. The sister has been receiving the [dawah], she's been very receptive; I can see in her eyes; she said she's about to accept Islam. And then he comes and he says she's not ready, and he says I know she's not ready, Subhan Allah, as if he can see the heart of a person, when she herself said she is ready to accept Islam.", "But the truth is, people like this are in Haram relationships, and they don't want the person to accept Islam, because if they do, they feel like that person is going to leave them, or going to start practicing properly and tell them: okay, let's get married. And they want to remain in that Haram relationship, and they don't want that headache. So they become a means of preventing others from accepting the religion of Allah. So whichever sins you're doing, do not be a means of pushing people away from Islam. We're trying our best to invite people, but then we have Muslims, sadly, people like this, who prevent others from accepting the religion with their behavior. Preventing someone from accepting Islam is, you can at least say, a major sin, if not even further. If you read what the scholars say about something like this, they would even say it can take a person away or out of the religion of Islam completely. May Allah guide us all.", "It's not about what you and me want. If she believes in the teachings of Islam, then essentially her belief is a Muslim belief.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sincere Lady About To Accept Islam But This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V2bQy_K4u5g", ((625, "10:25–10:53"), (653, "10:53–11:38"), (709, "11:49–12:01"),), id: 3432)

