#passage(("The truth is you can do that as a Muslim, and as a non-Muslim. Because in reality, let's say you read and you realise that everything was just a lie, you could easily come back to being something else! But within that period, let's look at it from a rational point of view: what are the benefits and what are the harms of taking that step and becoming Muslim, and following Islam right now?", "Benefit number one, you are following the Guidance of God, so it will better your life generally. So whether it is the prayer, which will give you serenity and peace in your heart, or whether it's the other commands of God that will improve your life generally, because it's the Guidance, the perfect Guidance that comes from God. So that's benefit number one. Benefit number two: if you die, you enter paradise, if you die upon that statement. Without that statement, you cannot enter paradise. This is the key. You've already done enough research to reach the point where you have the 6 Articles of Faith, which is the foundation. But if you say: \"Oh, I want to do this very long list of research,\" then you could die before! Anyone could die before. I could die before. But if you die after you do that, then that is a way for you to enter paradise. And third, there is no losing at all. Meaning: if you were to realise that things are incorrect, and the reality is not what you expected it to be, there's nobody who's going to stop you from changing your way.", "Now, what are the harms on the other side? Harm number one is Satan uses this idea. He will keep you in an infinite loop of research: this question versus this question, versus this video, versus this. It's just years and years of just going in loops and loops, not arriving to the destination. The second most very important problem is the fact that you're committing the Greatest Sin, which is to not affirm God, not to be a Believer in your life at the moment. And a consequence of that: if you were to die (and this is the