#passage(("Do you think there is a Muslim who doesn't sin? Impossible. The Prophet Muhammadﷺ told us: كُلُّ ابنِ آدمَ خطَّاءٌ (Every child of Adam makes sins). So, if you're waiting to stop sins before you become Muslim, that will never happen. Why? This life is a test. You're weak, I'm weak, we're weak. We'd fall, but Allah opened the door for repentance for us. We seek forgiveness. We ask Allahﷻ to forgive us. Then He forgives us and He opens the door for us. Allah, one of His names is He's \"The Forgiving.\" If we don't sin, how is Allah going to forgive us? God is perfect; we're not perfect; we're human beings. Allah says that if we didn't sin, Allah will remove us and bring a Creation that sins, and then He will forgive them, because He's The Forgiving, He's the Merciful. This is our nature; we make these mistakes. So leave this idea.", "You make tattoos, you kill someone, doesn't take you out of Islam. You're still a Muslim, but you are a sinning Muslim. But if you die today, Hellfire is your destination. If you die without accepting Islam: Hellfire, there's no other choice. But you accept Islam, you die, even if you're punished, you're going to go to Paradise eventually, because you died on Islam. And Allah said He made Paradise: no one will enter except the Muslims. So you do not delay something that will take you to Paradise, and you don't know when you're going to die. Some of my friends are saying, \"I'm going to get married...\" Years and years. You take your step, become a Muslim, then work on yourself.", "In Islam, we believe we have faith, something we call إيمان (Iman: faith). That faith increases and decreases. When you increase your faith, do you know what's going to help you? To leave all the sins around you, to practise Islam better, to be around a better company. So if you want to improve your life, you have to start by doing good deeds. You have to become Muslim and start doing good deeds. And when you do that, as I said to you, you will sin. Wallahi (I swear by God), if you become Muslim, even 100 years a [Muslim, you] will sin. The Prophet told us: there is not a human being that doesn't sin. Bring me one Muslim on this planet, in human history, that didn't sin. We are human, we are not perfect. If you are perfect, you can avoid to sin. You are not perfect, I'm not perfect. Even the Prophets of God, they did some things that God corrected them on. The Prophets of God! God chose them as the best people in humanity, the best creation among human beings, but they still made mistakes.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Emotional Shahada! Brother Accepts Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hvQ9biPlbos", ((34, "0:34–1:44"), (104, "1:44–2:29"), (153, "2:33–3:35"),), id: 3457)
// U ML099:443-505 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("You've already taken that step in your heart. It's not really about the Faith! So, it's not like you're not accepting Islam because you don't believe in Islam. No! It's you not accepting it yet because you're worried about what other people will say or what other people will do.", "All of us are deficient human beings; we make mistakes. We're not perfect, infallible in our actions. So should you be worried more about making a few mistakes here or there, or worried about not accepting God at all, and dying as a disbeliever and ending up in Hellfire? Which one should be more worrying? Because you're saying: \"I'm going to commit the biggest sin!\", which is Shirk (associating with God), \"so I can avoid committing maybe some sins, when I make mistakes.\" Do you see the irrationality of the thing?", "I'm not pressuring you in any way. If you feel like you're ready, you can. If you feel like you're not ready, then it's up to you whenever you want to take it. Like I say always to the people, I'm getting nothing, whether you accept Islam or not. So, I'm not getting anything from that. But I know that Islam is the Truth. And that's why two things: 1/ I want good for you, and 2/ The Creator commanded me to spread that good to people.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Shockingly Describes Life After Death Like You Are Witnessing It! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lePF6KO1aZA", ((1310, "21:50–22:08"), (1358, "22:38–23:11"), (1414, "23:34–24:08"),), id: 3458)
// U ML222:157-195 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("Satan says to them: you have to be perfect first, you have to follow everything the right way. No one is like this. I make sins and mistakes; everyone makes [sins] and mistakes. But Allah told us in the Quran what He asked from you is to do your best, as much as you can. But you will fall always; that's why we have repentance. Why is repentance there? If we can become perfect and do everything the right way, there's no need for repentance. Repentance is there because the prophet told us every child of Adam will commit mistakes, and the best among those who commit mistakes are those who repent. The best among us are those who repent, say: \"Oh God, forgive me, I did wrong, I try my best.\" I come and seek forgiveness from the Creator. I don't intentionally think I'm going to come back again and sin, no, but sometimes you're weak; you're human. Allah says in the Quran the [human is] created weak. We're not perfect; we make mistakes; we got desires.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Surprises A French Man Looking For Answers! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=piz443ivKUc", ((310, "5:10–6:05"),), id: 3459)
// U ML123:321-403 | The Muslim Lantern | 4
#passage(("If you believe Prophet Muhammad is the Messenger of God, and you read it in the Quran, it makes sense to you that it's from God, what is preventing you from taking that step and actually implementing Islam, and being a Muslim in your life and your practises? Since, like you say, they're all coming from God, the God of Abraham, and they're all Messages from the Creator to us in the end, and Prophet Muhammad is just the last Messenger in this long line of Messengers, why not take that step and actually implement the teaching of God in our life? Allah tells you in the Quran to enter into Islam fully (alBaqara2:208), meaning enter into submission of God, and obedience, and practising in your life, and being good as much as you can, because you need the guidance of God in your life, and without it you'd be doing things incorrectly.", "So what is stopping you from taking that step and implementing Islam and faith into your life, which is only going to improve your life? You will get the benefit before anything else. God doesn't benefit from us, being Muslims or not being Muslims. GOD IS FREE FROM NEED. We are the ones who benefit from obeying the Creator, and doing as the Creator commanded and guided us. It's a very quick process for someone to enter into the fold of Islam, and then take a step-by-step, of course, completing the Quran and learning how to pray and all of that.", "What you say, almost every person before they accept Islam, they say. But let me tell you something interesting. This is, I would call it, the leftovers of Christianity. I'm being completely honest with you. Why? Because Christianity has this creed of pushing guilt deep in you: \"You're a sinner.\" \"You're not worthy of the glory of God.\" \"You're a terrible human being.\" Repeatedly, you're told that. So you get brainwashed. And when people leave Christianity and they try to explore Islam, this leftover of Christianity has a very very deep root in them. While in Islam, the image has always been clear. Allah created us this way. If Allah wanted to make us in a way in which we do not make sins, like the angels in Islam, we wouldn't have been this way. This life is a test. Of course we will fall. But the point is to come back, and repent, and come closer to God.", "We're not saying get a free card and do sins. But, in the same time, do your best! But you will fall! But then you stand up again, and try to repent to God, and come closer to the Creator. That is the Message of Islam, and that's how it's always been. So, ignore this influence of Christianity, because it's coming from an incorrect place. What matters is your sincerity towards God, and your willingness and your effort to obey God, and not to disobey Him, and not to do sins. If that is there, then you should take your step and become Muslim.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Non-Muslim Lady Questions A Muslim On Polygamy Then This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pL8KhAcUgn0", ((930, "15:30–16:03"), (967, "16:07–16:33"), (1031, "17:11–18:08"), (1106, "18:26–19:00"),), id: 3460)
