#passage(("By not accepting Islam, you are committing the biggest unforgivable sin. Every Muslim will commit sins eventually, but at least he believes in God and he has a chance of forgiveness from God. As I said to you, even if these major sins, God can forgive; it's up to Allah. But the point is you have to be a Muslim. Mercy of God is conditional in Islam. Just like in Christianity, the condition is to believe in Jesus; while they will claim it's not conditional, it's conditional. But it's conditional in Islam: to get the Mercy you have to be a Muslim.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Arab Christian Introduced To The Challenge Of The Quran! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n-flvFktgzU", ((1458, "24:18–25:11"),), id: 3462)
// U ML190:468-517 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("You don't do things right by doing everything perfect. That's not doing things right in Islam, because Islam says that nobody is perfect. Allah says in the Quran explicitly (atTaghabun64:16) فَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ مَا ٱسۡتَطَعۡتُمۡ (Fear Allah and do as much as you can. As much as in your capacity). The Prophet said \"Whatever I tell you, try to do as much as you can; whatever I forbid you, stay away from.\" Allah says in the Quran (alBaqara2:286) لَا یُكَلِّفُ ٱللَّهُ نَفۡسًا إِلَّا وُسۡعَهَاۚ (Allah does not overburden a soul except what it can handle). Allah in the Quran does not hold us accountable for the mistakes that we do that we did not know about, we were ignorant about, or things that we were forced to do. If you think that I have to do everything the way it is mentioned in the Quran, nobody has done that, and nobody will do that. Because if you were perfect, then you'd be god! You're not perfect for a reason, because you're a creation of God.", "Now if this is the case, if you want to do things the right way, do you know how you do things the right way? You accept the Message of God that was sent to you. Allah mentions people like you. Allah says in the Quran (ali'Imran3:113), (From people of the Book..), Allah says (they're not all the same). And (There are people of them) (who when they hear the Message of Allah, then they accept it, they submit to it) (Their eyes tear from the Truth from what they hear about the Messenger) (alMaida5:83). Allah mentions people like that, and then they submit to the Truth. So Allahﷻ mentions people who are sincere with themselves, and when they hear the Message of the Truth, they're not arrogant (alMaida5:82). This is the most important thing Allah says about them in the Quran: وَأَنَّهُمْ لَا يَسْتَكْبِرُونَ (They're not arrogant). (When they hear what was sent down to the Messenger, they accept it.)", "That is the way you do things the right way: that you follow the command of the Creator, what Allah has sent down to you, and you obey and do as much as you can. That's it! Take things step by step. It's gradual steps. Everyone is going through that journey. Nobody just jumps and does everything right. Nobody is doing everything 100% right. That doesn't exist. Islam doesn't command you to do that, does not require that of you.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Unitarian Christian Questions The Similarities Between The Quran & The Bible! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t9EQwV9zMIE", ((1664, "27:44–28:33"), (1721, "28:41–29:24"), (1768, "29:28–29:52"),), id: 3463)
