#passage(("I don't want to push you. I want you to do it yourself. I never push anyone to accept Islam, except if I see that person is ready. If someone for the first time learns about Islam, I say go read. There's many people who already read the Quran, know this. They're practising, they fast Ramadan, but they're not taking the step. Why? Shaytan is stopping them! You're thinking you've got a reason, but it's only Shaytan stopping you. There's nothing else stopping you from accepting Islam. You said forgiving the sins. I said you repent, Allah will forgive the sins.", "Don't worry, we all make sins. Bring any Muslim from the road. He's a Muslim still. We don't say to him, \"You're not a Muslim.\" Don't think: \"I'm going to leave everything, then I'm going to enter the faith.\" You think you're going to become \"god\": pure, perfect, and then you'll become Muslim? That's not Islam! Islam is: everyone makes sins, everyone makes mistakes. As long as you believe in Allah, you worship Allah, you don't worship other gods with Allah, you believe in Prophet Muhammad, you're still a Muslim. And everything will come eventually.", "You will never stop until your faith increases, and your faith will never increase until you become a Muslim. Of course, they are sins, they're bad things, but you will never be able to leave them because your heart is attached to them. Your heart is not attached to Allah, so you will never leave them until you attach your heart to your Creator. When you attach your heart to your Creator, the Creator will allow you to leave these issues. When you become Muslim, you will see. Right now, when you take the Shahada, everything changes. You believe already. You just need to say it. But the devil knew that the guy who will say it, Allah will forgive all his previous sins. You're going to be like a born baby again. Then you'll sin again, Allah will forgive you. That's why the delay is from the devil. Just accept if you're ready.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Emotional Shahada! Brother Accepts Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hvQ9biPlbos", ((670, "11:10–11:53"), (739, "12:19–13:08"), (838, "13:58–14:51"),), id: 3465)
// U ML287:332-405 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("The testimony of faith, of how someone enters Islam: you have to want to do that yourself, and you have to understand that this is a step now into: \"I believe in God, therefore now I'm going to practice what God have told me to do.\" It's not like just say, \"Okay, I believe in God,\" and then go back to my day-to-day life. You will still continue to sin, but Allah tells you to do your best, to try every day to improve yourself. So if you do that, you're ready to become Muslim.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Lady Receives Reality Check From A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xhWvuStGaKY", ((684, "11:24–12:26"),), id: 3466)
// U ML099:513-555 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("How wouldn't you feel guilty by waking up in the morning, and realising you're still not a Muslim? How does that not make you feel guilty as well, if not praying would make you feel guilty? Which one is a bigger sin in the eyes of God? Not taking the step of being a Muslim, or missing some prayers? So how do you feel MORE guilty for something that God views less than the thing that you're doing? How is it possible that you feel more guilty for something that, in the eyes of God, is a lesser sin than what you're already doing? It's just Satan's manipulation in your mind. That's it. It's nothing really more than that. Because you can see that it's not common sense what you're saying. It's not reasonable. So the only answer to it would be that Satan is just giving you these bad ideas.", "It's not about doing it for me. You take the step when you feel like you're ready to take the step. It's not about scoring points! I'm not here trying to score a point. It's not like we're from a football game, and I'm trying to defeat the other team. It's about YOU doing it, content, and knowing that what you're doing is the right thing. I'm just helping you by telling you the rationality of it.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Shockingly Describes Life After Death Like You Are Witnessing It! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lePF6KO1aZA", ((1485, "24:45–25:55"), (1565, "26:05–26:29"),), id: 3467)
// U ML311:348-384 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("To say one year, that is huge. Take your Shahada, and then take it again on that day with your friends; I don't see a problem in doing that. But the reason I say take your Shahada is to guarantee yourself that if you die you do not end up in Hellfire. So, saying that Shahada is not for this person or that person; it is to guarantee: if anything happens to me today, I have at least testified to what I believe in my heart. But to say that tomorrow, next year, next week, I would not advise that, because you're already practicing Islam! You're doing certain things that probably some Muslims are not doing to that extent. You pray with your friends, you do all of that. You're already practicing Islam. It wouldn't make any sense to waste all of those deeds, because Allah will not accept any Deeds from you unless you're a Muslim!", "Allahﷻ says it clearly in the (Quran9:54): \"وَمَا مَنَعَهُمْ أَن تُقْبَلَ مِنْهُمْ نَفَقَاتُهُمْ إِلَّا أَنَّهُمْ كَفَرُوا بِاللَّهِ وَبِرَسُولِهِ\" \"What prevented them from their charity to be accepted, except that they don't believe in Allah and his Messenger.\" So Allah would not accept the actions of individuals, because it's a condition for the acceptance of the prayer, the acceptance of Deeds, is that you be a Muslim!",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sincere Man Realises The Contradictions In Christianity! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CR6_RG9qdVM", ((1282, "21:22–22:20"), (1346, "22:26–22:37"),), id: 3468)
