#passage(("This Testimony of Faith, the Shahada, you cannot [weigh] with any amount of gold. You cannot weigh it with any amount of money. This is the key to entering the doors of paradise. But the most important thing is that we die upon this Testimony of Faith: that when we're leaving this life, we leave upon that faith and belief that there is nothing worthy of worship except God, and that Prophet muhammad is His Messenger, and that He sent all of those Messengers to us, and that the Quran is that Message from Him that we need to believe and die upon. Now if we do that, then we enter Paradise.", "You take everything easy: continue, finish reading the Quran, learning how to pray. Once you do that, and implement it in your life, Allah forgives ANY of the previous sins that you did. You have a very clean empty slate to the God. It does not matter what happened in your past. If you now move forward, do your best to obey The Creator, and do as much as you can, Allah will forgive your past.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Surprises Truth Seeker With Evidences Of Prophethood! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JOwaMQoXaBQ", ((1246, "20:46–21:14"), (1281, "21:21–21:40"),), id: 3469)
// U ML155:259-285 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("Many people who are living, who not come across the idea of Islam as well, if they die like this, they have a different [test] in the day of judgment. But God is not going to hold them accountable until they hear the message, they know the truth. So don't worry about the past. Even some people have tattoos; they worry about tattoos. Even if it will remain on your body, if you done it before Islam, then Islam doesn't require you to do anything.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Intelligent Students Ask Curious Questions About Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XLWOnl9JFok", ((572, "9:32–9:57"),), id: 3470)
// U ML269:172-194 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("You shouldn't ask people about their Sins, and whatever is my past before Islam is between me and Allah. الإسلامُ يَهدِمُ ما كان قبلَه Islam removes that which came before it. والتوبةُ تَجبُّ ما كان قبلَها The repentance removes that which was before it. التَّائِبُ مِنَ الذَّنْبِ كَمَنْ لا ذَنْبَ لهُ The person who repents from his Sin is like the one with no Sin.", "This has to be understood: once someone accepts Islam, we don't talk about their past; their past is their past. The صحابة (Sahaba: Prophet's Companions) were old people who accepted Islam. Everyone knows how the past was in the Days of جاهلية (Jahiliyya: Ignorance; Pre-Islamic era). No one was going around: \"Oh, but you were doing this before Islam,\" because that was before Islam! The Ignorance Days, The Pre-Islamic days, that's why that term is used. Because this is the past. A person becomes Muslim; now, as long as he sincerely became Muslim, and he's practising Islam, whatever he has done in his past is irrelevant. And these things that are private should remain between you and Allah anyways.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Ex-Muslim Girl Leaves Islam For LGBTQ!? Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ygry-0BaOFo", ((584, "9:44–9:59"), (627, "10:27–10:56"),), id: 3471)
// U ML403:172-213 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("When you repent, Allah forgives your sins, and Allah replaces your bad deeds to good deeds (alFurqan25:70). Imagine you rape, or you steal, or you do this. When you repent, Allah will not only forgive you, He will make these bad deeds good deeds. Because when you become Muslim, it's a form of repentance. That's why your sins are forgiven. Because you now repented from the evil; you stopped. You didn't believe in Allah, you repented from that sin and you started believing in Allah. That's what it means. That's why we say your sins are forgiven. But that is the case for every deed that you will do.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Emotional Shahada! Brother Accepts Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hvQ9biPlbos", ((382, "6:22–7:00"),), id: 3472)
