#passage(("It's the feeling of Satan. He's trying to be like: \"Don't do it! Don't do it!\" Because a lot of people get that. And once they take the Shahadah, they realise that there's a burden that is left [off] them, because that weight of sins and Satan pushing them is gone, the minute they take that step, and they find the courage to actually take that testimony of faith.", "But again, it's NO PRESSURE AT ALL! Because, I'll tell you the truth, whether you accept Islam, or you don't accept Islam, I'm not going to get 10 million in my account. It's for your benefit. It's for your Afterlife. The reason we invite people to Islam is because we want goodness for them. That's the whole reason in the end. So there's no pressure on you, but we tell you that which is good, in hope of you taking the decision which brings you closer to God. So I would 100% recommend you do it, meaning you take your Shahadah, your Testimony of Faith. And like I said, you will 100% continue to learn and study.", "So you focus on learning how to pray, so you implement, actually, gratitude to God in your life. Don't you want to be grateful to God for what he's given you in your life? Do you want the days to continue to go by, while you're not being grateful to your Creator? Or do you want to be grateful to your Creator, while you are every day living this life, and breathing, and getting provision from God, and getting health, and getting family, and all of these things?", "We believe that when you accept Islam, God will wipe the sins that you did in the past. But, again, no way a person is going to continue in that. The person will sin after all. You will fall. You'll say something bad to someone. You'll lie. Whatever that problem is that you will do, something will happen, sooner or later. And you might speak about someone behind their back. Whatever you will do, and then you will commit sins again. But the important thing, like I said, is the rewards that you're missing! And the gratitude that you're not giving to God at the moment. And that surety that if you die, you are in the place that you don't want to be in when you die. Nothing beats that!",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Non-Muslim Lady Questions A Muslim On Polygamy Then This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pL8KhAcUgn0", ((1344, "22:24–22:41"), (1367, "22:47–23:21"), (1413, "23:33–23:56"), (1472, "24:32–25:17"),), id: 3473)
// U ML297:369-414 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("You're feeling like you're leaving something behind. So it's about forgiveness. You're not leaving this idea of forgiveness in Islam. The idea is still there. You seek forgiveness from God and God forgives you, and the Bible teaches you to repent, to seek forgiveness from God. And that's what Islam teaches you to do, like in Ezekiel chapter 18, where it says to you that if a person commits a sin or makes a mistake, he goes back to God and he repents and he seeks forgiveness and God forgives him, and that person surely shall live (Ezekiel18:26-28). And that's what Islam teaches you.", "Now about the guidance, God guides you every day. That's why you pray 5 times a day and you ask guidance every day when you pray. We say: اهْدِنَا الصِّرَاطَ الْمُسْتَقِيمَ (guide us to the Straight Path) every day. So you're not leaving any of that. The idea of forgiveness is there, but the difference is you're not killing Jesus for the forgiveness; you're seeking it from God directly.", "Which one is more just? Leave what people are telling you, because people can tell you anything, but is it better, or is it more just, that God will save his Prophet and Messenger? Or do you think it's better to believe that he was killed, stripped naked on a cross, and then bled for you to have forgiveness? Why do you need any payment for God to forgive you? If there is a payment, it's not forgiveness anyways.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sister Cries After Realising Islam Is The Truth! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PtJpInP1jl8", ((1147, "19:07–20:02"), (1202, "20:02–20:15"), (1226, "20:26–20:47"),), id: 3474)
