#passage(("If you accept Islam, it will count. Because, as we said, you need to understand it's a condition for you to be a Muslim. So once now that condition is fulfilled, the good deeds in your past are there. The Prophetﷺ, he said to one of the Companions: أسلمتَ على ما أسلفتَ من خيرٍ (You become a Muslim and all of the deeds that you've done good are there). But you have to accept in order for that condition to be fulfilled. So once you accept Islam, then there is no issues; now your deeds are accepted, the deeds that you've done in the past, because the condition is now fulfilled, of faith, of belief. Now all of these deeds are there in your slate of good deeds as well.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sincere Man Realises The Contradictions In Christianity! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CR6_RG9qdVM", ((1629, "27:09–27:42"),), id: 3478)

