#passage(("I think that's a grave mistake that many people do. And the reason I call it a grave mistake is simple: because the people in the West already have biases and preconceived notions that are bad about Islam, because they're brainwashed by the media. They're brainwashed by their community and society. So when someone accepts Islam and he's excited about making a right decision of obedience to God and submission to Him, and you go to your family members, the first thing they do is to give you negative feedback. And that negative feedback is based on how much they've been brainwashed to hate Islam. And the negative feedback, the level of how negative it is, is based on how the family is.", "So, I always say to the people, that's not the right thing to do. Your religion is a personal choice between you and God. It is a choice between me and the Creator. If something makes sense to me, I follow it. Now, when I feel ready, and I'm not as much worried of the harm that can happen or the negative feedback that can take place, then I can make that decision. But just jumping straight after accepting Islam, you tell people – I will definitely advise you do not do that.", "So your courage can increase with time. Once you accept Islam, start practicing it. Practice it bit by bit in your life. This feeling of being scared is not going to be there as much.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Shockingly Describes Life After Death Like You Are Witnessing It! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lePF6KO1aZA", ((1108, "18:28–19:01"), (1144, "19:04–19:29"), (1176, "19:36–19:44"),), id: 3479)
