#passage(("I know a lot of sisters who I tell to keep it to themselves in the beginning. They accept Islam, they go tell their sisters! I had someone who did this. She came to me and she said \"I should have listened\", because her sister told her, \"I'm not going to talk to you\", or something like this. She didn't take it well. So I told her that it's best in the beginning that you keep it for yourself until you're establishing the faith and the religion, you're now able to understand your family's belief, you understand your faith and everything like that, and then if you feel you're ready to share, you should share it.", "But we understand the reason. The reason is that people think Islam is a bad thing, because they've not studied it, they've not learned about it or did not research it.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Curious Lady Grills Muslim With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2EcJiOmZI44", ((2015, "33:35–34:02"), (2057, "34:17–34:24"),), id: 3480)
