#passage(("Everyone who accepts Islam struggles with this, and especially Christian Eastern Orthodox or just Eastern Christians. They're holding on to their religion a lot more. I wouldn't say it is necessarily for rational reasons, but there are a lot more practicing. It's more a part of their identity and all that. They would go to church and do whatever, but in reality, you don't really believe and read. So, I completely understand. But just know that in the end, Allah is on your side, and He can see you, and that everyone else struggles with this.", "Muslims or not, your family can stop you from praying, even if they call themselves Muslims. And they forbid girls from wearing the Hijab, praying, and all of that. Shaytan can use anyone.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Romanian Christian Grills Muslim With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RCeSQlWHPxI", ((1757, "29:17–29:48"), (1803, "30:03–30:10"),), id: 3481)
// U ML053:57-173 | The Muslim Lantern | 8
#passage(("It reminded me of a verse of the Quran, Chapter:39 of the Quran (azZumar), verse:15. Allah says: فَٱعۡبُدُوا۟ مَا شِئۡتُم مِّن دُونِهِۦۗ (Worship what you will, other than Allah). If you want to worship something else, worship something else. قُلۡ إِنَّ ٱلۡخَـٰسِرِینَ ٱلَّذِینَ خَسِرُوۤا۟ أَنفُسَهُمۡ وَأَهۡلِیهِمۡ یَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِیَـٰمَةِۗ أَلَا ذَ ٰ⁠لِكَ هُوَ ٱلۡخُسۡرَانُ ٱلۡمُبِینُ. So Allah says the true losers are those who lose themselves and their families يَوْم الْقِيَامَةِ (on the Day of Judgement). That is indeed the true loss.", "So you're thinking about your family right now. Talking about losing your family, a concept of losing family in this worldly life: the real loss of family would be that I lose my family on the Day of Judgement. This verse is specifically talking about you: worship what you want, you want to be a Christian and be with your family and do what you want, it doesn't matter, you can do it, you can choose to do that. But you are going to be the real loser who loses himself and his family on the Day of Judgement. Because having my family members around me for a few years is not true gaining of those family members.", "Why did the Prophet Muhammadﷺ ('alayhi ssalatu wa ssalam: blessings and peace be upon him) spend years and years and years trying to call his uncle before his death, bringing him to Islam -who was protecting him- and did everything in his power to do it? Because he knows the true loss. Yes, his uncle is there, he's protecting him, he's there in the Dunya (worldly life). But that's not having your family. Having your family is having them with you in Paradise. That is the true winning. This life is: you have your family today, tomorrow you're losing one of your parents. The parents are older than you, get a disease, a sickness. You can die before them. They can die before you. They're gone! They're not there anymore.", "So the idea of losing one's family, we've got to understand: I can lose myself and my family, or I can first try to save myself, then do as the Quran says (atTahrim66:6) يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا قُوا أَنفُسَكُمْ -yourselves- وَأَهْلِيكُمْ نَارًا -then your family-. So I have two options. Option number one: I remain on disbelief, I worship whatever I want, I remain with my family in this life and I lose myself and my family in the Afterlife, because I'll have an eternal punishment. Or I choose option number two: I save myself, and I do whatever is in my capacity to save my family, after saving myself. Now, am I going to be able to guide everyone necessarily? No! But the question is, is saving myself and whoever I can, if I could, better? Or losing myself and my family in the Afterlife? Which option would be the rational option to take?", "In the end, you've got to understand, you accepting Islam is for YOU. What does God lose if you don't become Muslim? (azZumar39:7) Nothing! So when you think about it: OK, I'm going to do this, I'm going to lose this.. In business, they talk about this risk/reward factor type of thing: there's this risk, there's this reward. You've got to think about the reality. OK, you lose some things here in the Dunya. You lose some pleasures, some things that are given to you in this Dunya that you can't do, you're restricted in certain ways, some luxuries are not there. That's why it's a test, and that's why you get absolute and eternal paradise in the Afterlife (alBaqara2:155).", "So, if we really truly care about our family, we cannot live in denial ourselves, and then let our families live in denial, and then we pretend we care about them! If I know Islam is the Truth, there's no doubt about it, Islam is the Truth, it's from God, and all I'm going to do now is I'm going to pretend it's not, so I'm going to live in denial, and then I'm going to let my family go to Hellfire, because they don't know what the Truth is. I'm not going to help them, I'm not going to try to give them advice, I'm not going to try to give them the Message. And that is somehow better than me doing what is good for me? So you absolutely got to take that decision and take that step for yourself, and then, as Allah said, after you save yourself, then you try and save your family.", "Allah gave us so many examples in the Quran about Prophets. If you read the Quran: the wife of Noah, the wife of Lot (atTahrim66:10), the father of Abraham (atTawba9:114), the son of Noah (Hud11:42-46), the father and mother of Prophet Muhammad (Hadiths), and the uncle of the Prophet we just mentioned (Hadith). The uncles of the Prophet were trying to kill him (alMasad:111)! Family members of the Prophets, and they couldn't guide them, because Guidance is not in the hands of us (alQasas28:56).", "So we also have to approach this realistically. We're not better than the Prophets of God, and God's given us this example to tell us: you're not better than these Prophets of God. And it is possible, even not just as a family that is not a Muslim family like yours, even a Muslim family, like let's say my family: tomorrow one of my family members can leave Islam. What can I do? There isn't anything you can do to save them. Whether you're born in a Muslim family or a non-Muslim family, the possibility of some of your family members not passing the test is always there, because this life is a test! Not everybody is going to succeed. But we do what we can, and we call people to the Truth, and we ask Allah to guide whom we can ask Allah to guide.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Arab Christian Shares His Experience With Islam And Christianity! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEUpYAh5b3E", ((206, "3:26–3:59"), (241, "4:01–4:31"), (276, "4:36–5:06"), (310, "5:10–5:57"), (360, "6:00–6:38"), (403, "6:43–7:22"), (451, "7:31–8:00"), (482, "8:02–8:40"),), id: 3482)
