#passage(("What we do is we take everything gradually, step by step. That's why I advise many people who have family, for example, who might have an issue with them being Muslim, that they keep it to themselves in the beginning. And Allah mentions examples of this in the Quran, like someone who is from the followers of Pharaoh (Ghafir40:28). Allah says in the Quran: \"and a man from the people of Pharaoh يَكْتُمُ إِيمَانَهُ: he was hiding his faith\". So he was hiding his faith because Pharaoh would completely slaughter him if he knew. So if you have a reason, a beneficial reason, you could hide your faith for the time being until you get first grounded into what you believe. And then once you're ready, then you can engage with your family members. But there's a very easy thing to do as well, which is to bring your family members to someone who knows, who talks to them, because the cure of ignorance is information.", "This is what Satan does always. The people who are about to practise Islam, he says \"oh, what about this? What about this?\" But I need to first ground myself. I need to first think about myself. Where am I? Before I start thinking where are other people.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Baha'i Lady Questions Muslim On The Last Prophet! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5_h1_yrAXLg", ((1235, "20:35–21:25"), (1294, "21:34–21:43"),), id: 3486)
