#passage(("Allah says in the Quran (Luqman31:15) that even if your parents are not Muslims, you should be good to them. But then, we say that you don't need to tell your parents when you become Muslim. There's no obligation on you. Imagine that I died, and I stand before God, and He says to me \"Why didn't you accept the Truth?\" And I say \"OK, my father didn't like it\". Would God accept that as an excuse from me? No! He would say to me: you feared your father or your mother more than you feared Me! The One Who created you. So, we put God first.", "There are a lot of sisters who accept Islam. When they're ready, they go, and they try, in the best time or the best situation. Then they say to their parents that they've accepted Islam. And most of the time -in the beginning- there might be a backlash, but then they adapt to them, because they understand it's your choice. And if I'm really a supportive parent, I should support you to do what is good for you. When you start practising, you will see the Faith growing in your heart, and you will want other people as well to adopt it, because it's good for them.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Priests Force Their Beliefs?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SU-3La7AfR4", ((754, "12:34–13:09"), (789, "13:09–13:52"),), id: 3489)
