#passage(("Prophet Muhammad had his parents die very early on. He didn't grow up with his parents; he grew up as an orphan. He grew up first with his grandfather, who passed away, and then he grew up with his uncle. His uncle did not accept Islam, and Allah revealed to him that you do not guide the ones you love. A man came to prophet Muhammad and he asked him: where's my father in the afterlife? He said: your father is in hellfire. That man got upset, was sad, so then the prophet said: my father and your father is in the hellfire, don't be sad.", "Abraham, peace be upon him: his father was [a disbeliever]. He would speak very gently, nicely with his father, and then his father would threaten him: I would kill you if you don't stop. So then he had nothing to do. He had no control. Lot: his wife. Noah: his wife and his son. His son, the story of the ship: everything is drowning, and he said to his son, \"Come.\" His son refused. He said, \"No, I'm going to go up a very high mountain. I'm going to be fine.\" He said to him, \"Nothing will stop you today.\" And then he died, cuz he was a disbeliever. Disobeyed his father. He didn't want to be a believer. The only thing that we can do is to be gentle and kind and be better people.", "So if your parents don't know you're converted yet, if they are very strong enemies of Islam or they don't like Islam or they hate Islam, then I would recommend you don't tell them about religion right now, at the beginning of your practicing. However, Islam makes you a better person overall. They will see that. And I think that is a bigger statement than any speech that you could say to them. [What] Islam says to you about how you deal with your mother: if you implement that as you should, if they start seeing that, all of a sudden you're the best person to your mother. You take care of her, you look after her, you're really helping her, buying her gift. She's like, what is going on? But she's happy about the change, because it's a positive change. I think it's the biggest statement that you can make towards your parents, not to say to them anything right now. Show them in your actions. Show them what Islam is, because they hear a lot of bad things about Islam. Show them how Islam is in application, and they will be curious themselves. They will know something change, and they will approach you. Then, after they see the good effect, you can be like, \"Yeah, I became Muslim. I believe, alhamdulillah, it made me a better person.\" And if they have any questions, you can answer. You can bring them someone of knowledge you can speak to. If you don't know the answer, you tell them I'll get back to you.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “How Do You Know Which Religion Is From God? A Detailed Comprehensive Analysis | The Muslim Lantern”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9F5gS1yWIRI", ((3452, "57:32–58:22"), (3515, "58:35–59:53"), (3604, "1:00:04–1:01:19"),), id: 3490)
