#passage(("So the question is, he accepted Islam 5 years ago. If it's 5 years ago, I don't think it's a problem for you telling him you're a Muslim, if you know him and you know that he's going to have a positive impact. Because you want good for him: if you want good for him, then you should invite him to Islam. If he has a good positive attitude towards the religion, then I definitely think you should tell him and invite him to Islam, give him some proof, some evidences. However, also, if you're having a circle of other non-Muslim friends, that this may come back and he goes and tells them and then there's an issue, then you need to weigh the benefits on the harms. But either way, I'll advise you to have Muslim friends in the end, and to speak to him, and even if it causes issues with other people, you have a good Muslim circle of friends around you.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “How Do You Know Which Religion Is From God? A Detailed Comprehensive Analysis | The Muslim Lantern”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9F5gS1yWIRI", ((5287, "1:28:07–1:28:51"),), id: 3491)
