#passage(("I would say that in Islam, when it comes to the practicing elements, Allah knows you and sees you! If you're afraid to pray because you're worried, you don't need to tell anyone after you accept Islam. So if you're afraid that someone is going to kick you out of the home or going to mistreat you, or going to do something if they see you, and because of that, you only pray when you can, Allah sees that! And He understands that. And He knows that. Until you reach a time where you're able to take your own decisions without worrying about someone else threatening you. Because in the West, they preach to us 24/7 about free choice and liberty, and free speech, and all of this stuff, but they don't care if it's Islam. If it's Islam: \"No! it's bad! Don't let your children..\" or don't let anyone practice their free speech and freedom to accept what they know is the Truth, and what they believe is the Truth.", "So, you can take your Shahada, and you can do whatever is in your capacity. Allah says in the Quran (AlBaqara2:286): لَا يُكَلِّفُ اللَّهُ نَفْسًا إِلَّا وُسْعَهَا (Allah does not overburden a soul except what it can handle). So, whatever is in your capacity, whatever you're able to do, Allah is going to hold you accountable for that. Nothing more, and nothing less.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Shockingly Describes Life After Death Like You Are Witnessing It! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lePF6KO1aZA", ((973, "16:13–17:06"), (1029, "17:09–17:24"),), id: 3492)
