#passage(("It was a realization just one day, and I'll tell you something interesting, and I think it's very important for a lot of people to do. One thing that clicked this journey of realization for me is that I used to spend a lot of time on social media, games or this or that or whatever it is. But for some reason, I don't remember the specific reason right now, the internet was not working for like a couple of days. So you were someone who were removed from social media for two days. You were removed from essentially what we call distractions. This is why a lot of people never think about the afterlife, never really think about why they're here: because they're distracted 24 hours; there's something distracting them. Either a friend, either a family member, either games, either money, whatever it is, their work, their next bill, their wife. Things are taking them away from thinking about the important things, which is: why am I here? What's my purpose? Why am I doing what I'm doing? Why am I making this money? Where am I going to go?", "So for me, being separated from the internet was a big part of me going through that journey of thinking. Because you have time, and when you have time, you can think about important things in life, what you're doing and this and that, and you're not wasting your time. But the more busy you are, the less you will be thinking about these important questions. So I would essentially say, this was my journey, in a short format. This was a trigger for me, if you want to say there's a trigger. But, essentially, we say that guidance is only from Allah. So I was guided because Allah عزَّوجَلََّّ guided me. That's it. Allah puts it in front of you, the options, Allah puts it in front of you the chances, and then he sees whether you're sincere enough to pick and follow these things or not.", "Even though I was just five, six, seven, eight, nine, ten years old, when I used to go and listen to the scholars, I used to enjoy it. Even one day, my brother, he said to me, come, let's play. And my father, he wanted me to go to the mosque with him. And I was so.. you know this meme where you don't know which red button that you click and you're sweating? This picture where someone who is sweating, he doesn't know which choice to make. I was in that position. Should I go to.. because I like going there. Even though my brother is: come let's play. I'm 10 years old or 12. But I used to love it. This was one of the things for me.", "The understanding of that guy who wanted to become Muslim: what was stopping him from the truth was the idea which is sinning, and he would think that he's a hypocrite because he's following Islam, but at the same time sinning. I think this is one of the biggest traps of the devil.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Why Are You A Muslim?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yUKKmAWojnc", ((634, "10:34–11:22"), (685, "11:25–12:04"), (847, "14:07–14:39"), (1073, "17:53–18:12"),), id: 3497)

