#passage(("I'll give you the brief story. Let's say I was young. Obviously, I'm still young, but I'm saying when I was much younger, let's say I was 17, 18, something like that. You live like any teenager would live or any young person would live. You just live your life, and your parents teach you about religion. You try to do.. because you're born with it, because your parents tell you to do it, you do it. That's what most people do: \"Okay, pray five times a day.\" So you pray five times a day, and obviously you don't do it seriously, because your parents are telling you to do it, and you're still young and you don't understand any of these things, and you don't understand why you're doing a lot of the things. But I used to go with my father to lectures and hear scholars speak and stuff like that a lot. So I was young, and then I was living, as I said, a normal young life: playing games on the computer, whatever young people do. There's different types of games I used to play. Some of them were online, and some of them were just on the computer, just basic games, the very basic games that you play just on the computer without connecting with other people.", "One day I just had this.. it's a guidance from the Creator. So we believe Allah is the one who guides. So I had this realization of thinking about life. I thought, \"Okay, what do I want to be? What do I want to do in the future?\" I was around 17 or 18. And what I was thinking is, \"Okay, what is the purpose behind whatever I'm doing right now? So I'm playing games and doing stuff like.. What am I doing? Where am I going?\" So I thought, \"Okay, let me work, let me study, let me go to university and let me get a good job, and then let me make money.\"", "I was in a Muslim country. So I was thinking, as I said, \"Okay, let me study, let me get good grades. Okay, and then I'm going to get a job, and then I'm going to get money. And then what? Afterwards, what should I do? Let's say I make all the money I want to make.\"",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Why Are You A Muslim?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yUKKmAWojnc", ((130, "2:10–3:43"), (227, "3:47–4:12"), (297, "4:57–5:11"),), id: 3498)
