#passage(("What's interesting, I think, is how you find God in the midst of atheism, because Sweden is one of the most atheistic and depressed countries in the world as a result of that. So finding God there is very interesting, because you see the lack of the existence of God in that Community, which I think can lead you to the existence of God. Maybe that's what happened with you: your [fitrah] can become awakened, coming through all of these incorrect ideologies, or ideologies are trying to represent or replace the existence of a Creator in a way.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Chinese Revert Shares His Conversion Story To Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7yAJVFrfEBk", ((334, "5:34–6:03"),), id: 3499)
// U ML387:208-262 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("People in the society, they know. If they don't know, they'll find out at some point in their life that materialism is not going to give you contentment and peace. And I think people found out the most in the period of the lockdown, because in the lockdown people were taken away from worldly distractions. There's no longer distractions. So most people would be like: why am I here? The existential questions will start coming up when you're no longer distracted with the world. The Fitrah (natural disposition) is going to overcome your position. So then it's either someone will turn into depression, not knowing what's going on, or Allahﷻ will guide them to the Truth, if he's a sincere person seeking the Truth.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “American Revert Asks Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2x1ZhIz1Hrw", ((615, "10:15–10:55"),), id: 3500)
// U ML363:1-252 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("In Islam you don't have to change your name, but it is good, it's not bad, it's a nice thing to do. Maybe sometimes it's a sign of completely denouncing the past and then coming with a new page.", "People try, I think, to forget what they saw in the war, what they saw in these places, by drinking, or women, going to materialistic.. just completely forgetting, but it never helps.", "Because you said you don't eat pork, they thought you were Muslim automatically. Which is an interesting thing, because this tradition is in Jewish tradition, some Christian Orthodox do it, but the people who are actually known to keep this tradition and practice it properly are the Muslims.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Ex-British Soldier Accepts Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MpAukyAbS_4", ((7, "0:07–0:14"), (102, "1:42–4:25"), (572, "9:32–9:39"),), id: 3501)
// U ML026:356-399 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("When I say that Allah Azza wa Jal is the healer, not you, I remember this story. This story is from a sister that accepted Islam, her and her daughter. They reverted. She sent me this 2 years ago. She says, \"How I accepted Islam: the quick answer is that my daughter had something giving her nightmares, and I saw Allah deliver when she cried out to him. That made me a believer. The story goes as every time my daughter closed her eyes to relax, wake up, or sleep, it would torment her. It looked like some kind of scary movie demon.\" So, when she closes her eyes, she would see something like a scary movie demon. \"Once while meditating\" – and that's why we tell you that meditating and these actions are acts of worship. This yoga, it means to unite yourself with the universe. That's actually what the word means. It's acts of worship. And that's why a lot of the people that do these acts of meditation, reiki, and all of this stuff, they get jinn possession, because they are doing wrong and haram practices. However, let's come back to this idea.", "\"Once while meditating with our eyes closed, we both saw it come into the room\" – her and her daughter saw it – \"come into the room and run up to her and stare in her face.\" Now, imagine a shaitan comes up to your face and stares in your face. That's what she saw. This was before she accepted Islam, her and her daughter. \"Since my eyes were closed, I opened them and saw my daughter crying in fear. We had seen the same thing.\" Both of them, when they closed their eyes, they saw that jinn. \"I prayed to the Christian God, but there was no answer. I was not a believer in the Trinity, but I did believe in God. I spoke to someone who said they were an astrologist and told us to pray to Kali, a Hindu goddess. That didn't do anything. I put crystals in her room, burned sage, and did a lot of things, but nothing worked. Then one night this unusual feeling came over the house, and a sense of peace.\" It's very important. \"I was in my room alone when it happened. Before I could call for my daughter, she opened the door of her room and yelled out, \"Allah is the only God.\" He got rid of it. She told me that when she was praying, she felt like she needed to call out to Allah, and so she did, and then it left. I believed right then that Allah must be God almighty to do something like that. I had been feeling called to Islam since I was about 16, but had been too scared to let my family down, since I was involved in a Christian ministry at one point in my young life. That all happened about a year ago. That thing has never been back since.\"", "This is where the idea when we say Allah Azza Wajjal is the healer. Believing in Allah Azza Wajjal, humbling yourself to Allah, calling out to Allah, this is what you need to understand. This is what gives you true healing. This is how a person would heal themselves. So, that is what you need to internalize when we talk about someone who's having [sihr], ain, or evil eye, or any of these things.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “How To Protect Yourself From Jinn, Possession, Magic & The Evil Eye In Islam - Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dDdEEnJpWmI", ((1321, "22:01–23:06"), (1388, "23:08–24:45"), (1488, "24:48–25:08"),), id: 3502)
// U ML116:141-176 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("You shouldn't feel guilty, because Allahﷻ can test us in this life, and Allahﷻ can give us reminders and signs through difficulty. People sometimes lose their own family members, and that is how they find God. They find Allahﷻ through losing a family member. They love someone so much, dearly, but when that person is gone, it's a wake-up call to them that this life is NOT forever. Everything precious here is coming to an end; it's never going to stay forever.", "So, especially from our side as Muslims, nobody is going to hold anything against you. In fact, we're happy that people are seeing the Truth. We're happy that people are learning what's going on, because before that, there was a lot of lies that were being spread – making the good people look like they are the bad ones – through the people who own the media, have the money, and own the banks and all of this stuff. But today, people are coming to the realisation that this is not the case anymore. So, we are grateful for that. And as long as the person is sincere enough to come to the Truth, Muslims are always welcoming and happy for this.", "Allahﷻ says in the Quran to the Companions of the Prophetﷺ (anNisa4:94) (If someone comes and gives you greetings of peace, do not say to them, you're not a believer). Then Allahﷻ says something to the Companions: كَذَٰلِكَ كُنتُم مِّن قَبْلُ (This is how you were before). So, Allahﷻ says to those Companions: you were disbelievers once (Then Allah has given you the favour of becoming believers). So, it's a blessing and favour from Allahﷻ that He's guided us. Someone did not had the guidance, and then, through whichever means, he found the guidance. This is a blessing from Allahﷻ. And there is nothing to blame. We're not going to blame that person for not finding guidance from the beginning, because this life is a test. Nobody was born and Allahﷻ then told them at birth or something: OK, this is the Truth. No! The life is a test, and throughout this life, when you come of age, then you start learning about things, then you either come to the Truth -which a part of it is innate- or you are going to choose falsehood. So, when people become guided, we're always happy for this.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Emotional Shahada | Peruvian Sister Discovers The Truth Of Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PZDTz4a-nZA", ((530, "8:50–9:18"), (562, "9:22–10:03"), (608, "10:08–11:10"),), id: 3503)
