#passage(("If you believe what Islam teaches, then I think you should take that step and accept Islam. And then the learning is something everyone does. I do, and every Muslim does, which is to learn about more. So you'll continue reading the Quran and you'll learn how to pray. Start learning how to pray and start praying every day, getting closer to the Creator, and learning more and more on a daily basis.", "And accepting Islam is a very simple thing, by the way. You do something called the Shahada. Shahada is to testify there is nothing worthy of worship except Allah. That's what you're going to say. And you're going to say that Prophet Muhammad is his Messenger and servant. And that's it! There's only One Creator, One God, with the definition that we said, which is Allah, worthy of worship; nothing else is worthy of worship except God: no saints, no Prophets, no human beings. And then you will say that Prophet Muhammad was sent by God as the last Messenger in the line of all of the Messengers that we said: Moses, Noah, Abraham, Jesus, all of them. Once you say that, you become Muslim. It's as simple as that. You just testify. You say that in English and Arabic. And then after that, you learn.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Questions Muslim On The Education Of Women In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K1ADYkUV9-Q", ((1315, "21:55–22:17"), (1343, "22:23–23:05"),), id: 3512)
