// U ML289:602-660 | The Muslim Lantern | 6
#passage(("I think you're saying some Arabic words beautifully, so we'll start with the Arabic now. Usually I start with the English with the people.", "It is a beautiful thing always to come back to the Truth, as long as it happens before our death. Then if we die upon Islam, then we have succeeded. That is the most important thing.", "There's something called the Fitrah: it's an innate disposition Allah created you with, it's pure. And because it's pure, perhaps it's because of how your parents raised you, they didn't raise you in falsehood from the beginning. So you have a pure natural disposition, therefore it is receptive to the Truth. Whenever it encounters the Truth, it recognises the Truth, which is something very beautiful.", "As I always say to the people, Allah is the one who guides. Allah is the one who guided you through the situation happening in Palestine. He guided you through that way and He guided you to come back to doing your research, He guided you into doing everything you do. You knew that thanks that you gave your way is not enough, because that's not what Allah wants from you. God didn't ask you to thank him this way; he asked you to thank him in a different way. And if you want to thank Allah, it has to be in accordance with what He wants you to thank Him with, or you're not thanking Him, you're thanking yourself, because you're using your own method. So deep down you knew that this was not sufficient.", "Allah is الكريم, He's The Most Generous, and He is الرزاق. He gives provision even to the disbelievers, those who disbelieve in Him, who curse Him; He's still giving them water, he's still giving them food, he's still giving them air. So on the Day of Judgement, none of them can say I didn't have a chance. Everyone had a chance, everyone had a life. If you want to talk about patience, there's no one Who is more Patient than Allahﷻ upon His servants and slaves.", "When you accept Islam, previous sins are forgiven, but you have to take Islam