#passage(("Now you take everything gradually. Life is a gradual journey. You used to believe some things and you start believing other things. You discover. You learn. You take things gradually. Step by step. That's how life is.", "And I will connect you with people. Because we have people also, I'm sure, in the country that you're in, and people who can communicate with you online: learning how to pray, the basic questions, the things that are to do with Islam. Because everyone needs someone in the beginning of their journey to help them take steps.", "And this is the thing, the beautiful thing about Islam: it betters you as a human being. A lot of people don't understand. They don't know that. But practising Islam, living Islam, it just makes you a better human being in general.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Scandinavian Man Surprises Muslim With A Difficult Question! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mf3NbKmeOt8", ((938, "15:38–15:48"), (965, "16:05–16:16"), (1002, "16:42–16:50"),), id: 3540)
// U ML057:1291-1340 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("So it's really one thing you should focus on in the beginning, which is to learn how to pray. While you're reading the Quran and understanding it, reading translations, you need to learn how to pray. That's the main focus that you need to focus on. You learn how to pray, and once you learn how to pray, you learn the other traditions of Islam, which is the charity given, the fasting and the pilgrimage, the pillars of Islam. Just take them one by one, but start with the prayer, because you did your shahada.", "Once you understand these main basic things, then you can delve into more understanding of specific details of things, like more [exegesis] of the Quran, what the hadith is, with the explanations of scholars, stuff like this. Take your time. Don't delve into so much information where you go everywhere and start getting confused; a lot of people do that. And also don't overburden yourself with so much: oh, this is haram, I do this, I do that. No. If you do all of this, things become difficult: can I do this, can I do that? Take things a bit by bit, slowly.", "And if you hear something from someone, it's very important: don't just take the word for it. A mistake that a lot of [reverts] do, they're like, \"Okay, this guy is born a Muslim, or this girl is born a Muslim. She must be right. If she's born in Islam, then what she's telling me, she must know what she's talking about.\" No, there's ignorant people in every tradition. They need to either be trusted, respected people of knowledge, or they're giving you evidences, like they're showing you verses of the Quran and hadith and stuff like that. But mainly it should be people of knowledge, people who are trusted.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Lady Grills Muslim With Questions Then A Surprise Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JOpckbnPmsM", ((3939, "1:05:39–1:06:09"), (3987, "1:06:27–1:06:54"), (4014, "1:06:54–1:07:27"),), id: 3541)
// U ML289:513-529 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("And know that you cannot go wrong when you become Muslim, because if you follow someone who told you something, and you believe it is good, and it was not good, you're not punished for it, because you did your best for trying to find the Truth, so you are safe from that perspective. From second perspective: whatever you try to learn, if you're doing your best, it does not matter how long it takes, Allah does not hold you accountable, because you are trying your best to learn, so you're safe from that level and perspective. Thirdly, if you do something wrong, that Islam says is wrong, but you do not know it's wrong, there is no accountability on you. Allah does not hold someone accountable for something he doesn't know.", "So when someone becomes Muslim, he's safe from all aspects. He's got nothing to worry about. All he needs to do is to actually put his effort in learning and trying to get as much information as possible from people that seem reliable and reasonable.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Popular Youtuber Asks Muslim Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S7bA8bsNs20", ((1877, "31:17–31:47"), (1909, "31:49–31:57"),), id: 3542)
