#passage(("You need to shut the door of questioning whether you've done the right or the wrong thing, because Satan will try his best now to tell you you've not done the right thing; he'll try his best to put anything in front of you. So I would say it's a good thing for you to do now: I would put a nice recitation of the Quran for 30 minutes to one hour and listen to them. And then tell your friends, the Muslim ones, that you accepted Islam, and go with them to the Mosque. This is what I would do, if I were you: tell them you become Muslim, look how they react, and tell them that you want to learn how to pray and all of that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Challenges Muslim On God Then This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MSk1AiEaXH8", ((3307, "55:07–55:54"),), id: 3543)
// U ML397:288-316 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("I want you to read the Quran. Take your time reading the Quran. Because reading the Quran, you'll understand more what Islam teaches. Why does it make sense? What is going to happen to me when I die? Is there a purpose in this life? It will answer all the questions that you have throughout reading it.", "But I'll tell you this. You've done the right thing. Why have you done the right thing? Because you did it for Allah, you did it for the Creator. And if I was just lying to you and telling you some nonsense, tomorrow you say, \"I'm not gonna accept this.\" So, if someone is not telling you the Truth, tomorrow you're not gonna follow; but if I'm doing that, then I'm the stupid one, because I know tomorrow you're going to leave, what's the point? But the point is, I know this is the Truth, I know this is from the Creator.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Why Should I Accept Your Religion?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rBgIryv7XPM", ((773, "12:53–13:15"), (808, "13:28–13:51"),), id: 3544)
// U ML087:328-366 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("Allah leads people who are sincere, people who take the step, people who do research. And Allah guides you to the Truth in the end! If you're researching, if you're learning, if you're spending your time, Allah says (those who struggle in Our way, We will guide them) (alAnkabut29:69). Allah will guide you, if you struggle to find the Truth.", "And once you accept Islam, Allah forgives any sins that you had in the past. You have a clean slate. Anything good that you've done, Allah keeps in your account. And from now on, practice Islam. Don't pressure yourself. Nobody is perfect. I'm not perfect. I commit sins. You would commit sins. Everybody commits sins. Nobody is infallible. Nobody is away from committing any sins or doing anything bad. So, if you live your life understanding that, and you take things step by step, that's how you should do it.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Truth Seeker Presents Muslim With Genuine Questions About Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fbAbWBPDY6M", ((837, "13:57–14:11"), (853, "14:13–14:52"),), id: 3545)
