#passage(("This statement of Faith is two words: simple words, two statements, but they mean EVERYTHING. They mean our existence, why we're here in this life: is that there is nothing worthy of worship except Allah, and that the Prophet Muhammad is the last and final Messenger in a long line of Messengers. That's what these statements mean! And through believing in them, and dying upon them, is the most important thing. Keep living upon them, and dying upon them. Until you die believing in them, is the key to entering Paradise.", "Don't let Satan play this game with you of guilt trip. And what I say to people when they accept Islam: if you do something that is wrong because you're forced to, because you're worried your parents will kick you out or this or that, it's NOT a sin! Because you're forced and compelled to do. You're only sinning when you're choosing to do something when there's nothing preventing you, or there's nothing forcing you, and you're choosing to do it, knowing that it's a bad thing. So, Allah will take things with you step by step. Allah is Merciful, and everything will work out if you do it for God.", "Of course, you will be tested! I'm never going to tell you everything is going to be easy and butterflies! Allah says (alAnkabut29:2) (Do people think..?). There will be tests in life, there will be difficulties, but in the end, if you are with Allah, you'll be content. That is the most important thing.", "You can wash your whole body with water, which is similar to غُسل (Ghusl: Major ablutions), and that is recommended after you accept Islam, because you have internally purified yourself, you externally purify yourself as well, and then you can pray. Pray to Allah. You can thank him for taking that step, and making that decision.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Shockingly Describes Life After Death Like You Are Witnessing It! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lePF6KO1aZA", ((1864, "31:04–31:26"), (1898, "31:38–32:08"), (1934, "32: