#passage(("Prophetﷺ said to us: إِنَّ الدِّينَ يُسْرٌ، ولنْ يشادَّ الدِّينُ إلاَّ غَلَبه (verily the religion of Islam is easy and no one fights with the religion except that it pushes him out). So the people who make things difficult for themselves, then things become difficult for them, but Islam is easy. It's a natural thing. You were born, you're disposed to believe in that; Allah has put that in you when you were a baby. He's a Prophet of God, he called to worshipping One God Alone, he called the same Message of all the Prophets of God, He demonstrated with evidences that he is a Messenger and a Prophet of God; therefore why not accept it.", "And you read the Quran, you will learn. Trust me, the more you read the Quran, the more you know. If you do 2 pages 5 times, I believe you'll finish it in two months, the whole Quran. Quran in 600 pages, but I'm talking about the Arabic by the way. I don't know about the English if it's a bigger or no, but the English is not going to be that bigger. So if you do 2 pages after 5 times a day, 10 pages a day, you don't have to, but if you do that you'll finish very quickly; it's not going to take you a long time to finish the Quran. My advice is: take your pace, and actually reflect on what it says, because some people, they just read completely quickly.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Intelligent Man Examines The Evidences For Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CyXdIF4BXok", ((2481, "41:21–41:47"), (2563, "42:43–43:30"),), id: 3548)
// U ML370:71-127 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("There's nothing that makes Muslims happier than to see someone who's, we believe, saved: someone who's closer to enter Paradise, someone who if he dies upon his belief he will enter Paradise. There's nothing more happier for us as Muslims.", "Always know that the religion represents itself, not the people, because sometimes you might have bad experiences with the people. The religion represents itself, is the Truth, it's from Allahﷻ. And there's millions, billions of brothers and sisters who are happy that you're a Muslim, and they will help you in anything that you need.", "And what you just did makes a lot of people angry, people who hate Islam. All these guys become Muslims, they're not happy to see that, but Allahعزوجل is the one who guides. No matter how much people hate the Truth, there will always be people coming to the Truth on a daily basis.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Surprise Shahada! Jack Accepts Islam! | Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xFtA1vLQqls", ((290, "4:50–5:07"), (372, "6:12–6:24"), (384, "6:24–7:10"),), id: 3549)
// U ML147:534-564 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("And sincerity, it's a very admirable characteristic. And the reason I told you the Quran is because I wanted your raw reaction. Because remember, I told you about confirmation bias? If I told you it's the Bible, then you'll instantly try to find the reason to respond. But when you realise, OK, the confirmation bias is not going to come out, you'll give your objective raw opinion when I tell you that this is what the Quran says. So it's very important. Keep company with your friend.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Left In Utter Shock After Attempting To Criticise Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cFKbacM6CFs", ((1395, "23:15–23:44"),), id: 3550)
// U ML271:434-464 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("We as Muslims need to always understand this: Forgiveness is in the Hands of Allah. We are not the ones who determine who we forgive or who we don't forgive. We are not the ones who say \"OK, you did this in your past, we're not going to forgive you.\" This is not in our hands, only Allahﷻ.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “IDF Soldier Confronted A Muslim Live Then THIS HAPPENED! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-qnYJXIxSpc", ((1448, "24:08–24:26"),), id: 3551)
// U ML006:898-967 | The Muslim Lantern | 4
#passage(("I think the biggest issue that reverts battle with when they accept Islam is they overwhelm themselves with too much information. They have a lot of fear. They think: I'm doing this right? I'm doing this wrong? I'm worried. Someone needs to tell me this. Am I doing this right? It's a misconception that Islam wants you to become the perfect Muslim the next day. Doesn't exist. You got many people that say to me, \"I can't accept Islam because I'm sinning. I believe Islam is the truth, but I'm a sinner.\" I had a person who was like, \"I'm a tattoo artist. I [can't] become Muslim.\" You can become Muslim. Of course, nobody's perfect.", "Another thing is: don't think that you're an external person from this community or something. Don't think that people are going to look at you different because you're from a different race or a different color. You can see everybody here sitting in all different colors and races and countries and ethnicities, and we're all one family, which is the family of Islam, family of being a Muslim. So don't have that misconception.", "Now when it comes to other misconceptions, of course that will be person dependent: some people have some misconceptions depending on where they grew up or what they heard from other people. Another misconception is: you have to learn Arabic. Oh, I have to learn Arabic to be a Muslim. No, you don't have to learn Arabic. Over 80% of Muslims [are] non-Arabs. Many of them don't even know the Arabic language. Only some things need to be done Arabic, like the prayer, reciting the book of Allah, because the speech of Allah, you have to recite it original language. But other than that, do you need to learn the Arabic language? Absolutely not. Is it good? Of course. But you don't need to.", "Another quick misconception is: I have to change my name if I become Muslim. Now people are going to start calling you Omar or Abu Bakr. No, you don't have to, if your name doesn't have any issues, anything against the teachings of the religion. If my name is the servant of Jesus or something, or the slave of Jesus, you have a problem. Some people have these names in Arabic, [Abdul Masih], for example; you have to change that name because has negative connotations. But if your name is just like any average name, Luke, John, just an average name, you don't need to change that name. Just because you became a Muslim, it doesn't mean that you have to change your name. Because a lot of Muslims, they will come back: oh, what's your new name in Islam? You don't have to have a new name. Your name that you're born with is okay so long as doesn't have any issues with it.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “How Do You Know Which Religion Is From God? A Detailed Comprehensive Analysis | The Muslim Lantern”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9F5gS1yWIRI", ((3244, "54:04–54:39"), (3315, "55:15–55:37"), (3337, "55:37–56:13"), (3373, "56:13–57:03"),), id: 3552)
// U ML363:304-368 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("Some people are sincere in their actions. The minute they become Muslim, some sisters wear the niqab. An English sister becomes Muslim, and two weeks later she comes to us with a niqab, and we're shocked! She's wearing a full Burka, a full Niqab! But they take it more seriously. You take it more seriously because you've seen the opposite, the other perspective: people getting drunk in night clubs, starting fights, and that social media and everything else.", "Some people have this perception that Muslims force their religion on people. You came across the religion by yourself. You became a Muslim by yourself, and it is good for people to see and learn that Islam is like that. Islam is a religion that is for everyone. And if you are sincere and you actually do your research, you will see that the evidences are more compelling than anything else. It will have to lead you to the fact that this is from God, that this is the Truth, and we should all be adopting it and accepting it. I got a lot of people from Army. Surprisingly, they don't want to do what they tell them to do in the army, and they come back really interested in Islam.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Ex-British Soldier Accepts Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MpAukyAbS_4", ((830, "13:50–14:16"), (878, "14:38–15:17"),), id: 3553)
// U ML319:467-530 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("We have something we say: أَعُوذُ بِاللَّهِ مِنَ الشَّيطَانِ الرَّجِيمِ – I seek refuge in Allah from Satan. Because Satan is always trying to play with our minds, even Muslims. Allahﷻ told us that specific type of Satan (called Khinzab) comes to you in your Prayer to try to confuse you. He says to you, \"ok, you forgot your child\", \"you forgot you've done this\", \"you've done that\"; he try to make you completely confused and not focus on your worship to Allah. So Satan will have an influence on your mind when you're trying to learn or everything like that. It's just Satan playing games with you, trying to make you think \"no, no, don't do it\", because now you're sure this makes sense, this has to be for God, this is for me; then he's trying his best to stop you from taking that step.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sincere Romanian Asks Questions About Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eixflyogKg4", ((1564, "26:04–26:49"),), id: 3554)
// U ML222:441-464 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("Practice Islam: you do as much obligations Allah command you as possible, the five daily [prayers]. There's obligations, and then there is things which voluntary you can choose to do. You keep your obligations and try as much as possible to avoid the prohibitions. You will fall sometimes, you get lazy sometimes, but still you believe, and you try to come back, you try to correct yourself. That's how everyone does it.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Surprises A French Man Looking For Answers! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=piz443ivKUc", ((921, "15:21–15:45"),), id: 3555)
// U ML297:684-809 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("Whatever we do for God, God is not going to punish us for it; because you sincerely did it for Allahﷻ, not for anyone else.", "Islam is that which you cannot push on people. People have to make that decision on their own by wanting to do it. It's not something that you can force onto someone, because it's a belief and faith in the heart. Trust me, when you start practising Islam, you'll see the effects on your life, and when you look back you'll say, \"OK, why was I so scared?\" This is always what people say: \"Why was I so scared to take the decision?\"", "You did it when Allahﷻ planned that you do it, not when you planned that you did it. Allahﷻ paved the way for you to do it today. And I understand why it was a bit fearful for you; because you were taking Christianity seriously, and not many people do. That is why it felt like a big step to take.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sister Cries After Realising Islam Is The Truth! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PtJpInP1jl8", ((2160, "36:00"), (2195, "36:35–36:52"), (2332, "38:52–39:07"),), id: 3556)

