#passage(("God has given us what we call The Fitrah. Fitrah is this innate disposition that every human being has. When you hear this information, it makes sense, it's very simple, it's common sense, to the people they can already accept. Do you know how a person becomes a Muslim? They say something called The Shahada. Shahada is a testimony of faith. What is a testimony of faith? It is to testify \"There's nothing worthy of worship except Allah\", and to testify that \"Prophet Muhammad is his messenger and servant\". So if you testify to that, which makes sense to you, which you believe in, then this is how you enter Islam.", "Then you take your step-by-step to learn. Your life doesn't change 180 degrees. No one becomes a Muslim, next day, her or him, is doing everything; it doesn't work like that. And you don't change your life in one day. People, they accept and then they gradually learn. So it's a step by step process, baby steps, like they say. And then you reach your goal. But you don't jump from one place to another. That doesn't work. So you just get confused, overwhelmed with information. So when you become Muslim, focus on yourself, reading the Quran, focus on learning how to pray. That's what you should do.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “University Student Challenges Muslim On Religion! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0eOxOwACYXE", ((534, "8:54–9:29"), (574, "9:34–10:19"),), id: 3557)
// U ML315:49-82 | The Muslim Lantern | 5
#passage(("Our brother Sneako: since he accepted Islam, we can see that he's taken Islam seriously; he's taking Islam much more seriously than many other people who accepted Islam. You can see that he's trying to practice Islam, is trying to learn how to pray. He posts pictures of him when he's praying Jum'ah (Friday) Prayer. He went to Sheikh Othman, and you can see he did the Daawah, he went to streets and he did Street Daawah. And you can see in his message, he's trying to invite other people to Islam, is trying to give The Daawah, trying to do his best, step by step, to bring people closer to Islam. And I hope he continues in the same kind of path that he's taking, step by step learning a bit more and more about Islam, and taking things a bit easy, and not pushing himself too much.", "The first thing I want to mention is this idea of usury and interest, and whether it's Haram (Impermissible) or it's not Haram. Yes, usury is Haram. Interest is Haram in Islam, and there is a reason for anything that Allahﷻ says it is Haram.", "The people who are watching our brother Sneako, they need to understand that dealing with someone who's just accepted Islam is not the same as dealing with someone who's been Muslim his whole life. And also, the way that we give advice to someone has to be based on wisdom and has to be based on good speech. So our brother Sneako is just someone who's newly accepted Islam. You cannot just be, some people called \"Haram Police\", and all of the time, whatever you see of him, you just criticize him for it publicly. You need to understand that there is a gradual process to take step by step with individuals who just accepted Islam.", "Which is why our Mother 'Aisha رضي الله عنها (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: in the beginning of Islam, if Allah said to the people, don't drink and don't have sexual intercourse, people would not have accepted Islam. But Allahﷻ, out of His wisdom, He took a step by step, gradually prohibiting alcohol for the people; step by step, gradually teaching them about the afterlife first, until Iman and faith has increased in their heart. And then you can start telling them about all of the permissible and impermissible things. This is what Allahﷻ did with the people.", "Yes, I understand there are things which are Haram, and giving advice to our Muslim brothers and sisters, it's an obligation upon us. But the way we do it is very important; understanding the stage that a person is at, in his life, is also very important. A lot of people are ignorant: watching our brother Sneako, they're just criticizing him and attacking him. Even in the way that they are criticizing him, it is completely un-Islamic and incorrect.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “A Message To Brother Sneak∅ - Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qxPkIlR6sb4", ((98, "1:38–2:24"), (148, "2:28–2:35"), (167, "2:47–3:09"), (194, "3:14–3:33"), (218, "3:38–3:55"),), id: 3558)
// U ML315:162-204 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("So it's important to understand: not to worry too much about other people. All you should worry about first and foremost is Allahﷻ. You worry about Allahﷻ. Do not worry too much about what people are saying. People, they will continue to criticize. People criticize a lot. And when you have a question about whether something is permissible or not, ask someone of knowledge, and don't ask the chat, because the chat is not a good place for you to know Halal and Haram. Ask people of knowledge. You can speak to our Brother Uthman and ask him: is this permissible or impermissible? And he will walk you through a process, and alternatives, and what is Halal and Haram.", "And try to also surround yourself with people who are PRACTISING. I understand that's very difficult, because you are this kind of an influencer, kind of environment where it's very difficult to find someone who is practicing, who's a MUSLIM. My advice is: try to have at least few friends around you that are people who actually practice Islam, that you spend time with them. Because then you realize things are much easier; because when you are around people who are doing a lot of things that are Haram, then it becomes difficult for you. You feel like you are alienated, you're the only one who's not able to do these things. But when you have a good company around you, good friends, then it's very easy for you to see: OK, no, it's OK, not everything is Haram, because I'm with my friends and we do all of these things that are not Haram.", "And this is what we need to understand: our brother Sneako is trying his best. It's been, he said, 3 months he didn't touch alcohol, staying away from it. He's gradually trying to improve his life step by step, and he's calling people towards Islam. So we need to be gentle with him. Trust me, most of the things are Halal, but it's just you need to take things easy. In life you need to improve your life a bit by bit, you need to surround yourself with the right people, and not to worry too much what people online are saying. Allahﷻ is The One that should be your ultimate goal to please, no one else. Not the chat, not people watching you, nothing like that. And my advice is for the Muslims watching our brother Sneako: the way you advise him has to be very beneficial, or don't say anything, like The Prophetﷺ, he said (say good or remain silent).",), "The Muslim Lantern, “A Message To Brother Sneak∅ - Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qxPkIlR6sb4", ((527, "8:47–9:27"), (571, "9:31–10:00"), (625, "10:25–11:14"),), id: 3559)
// U ML318:1039-1068 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("[Nowhere] does the Quran or Sunnah teaches that a man MUST marry more than one wife. And that's why most of Muslims are not, over 95% are not. So this is, I would say, an irrational fear, because you can avoid it, by making that condition, stipulating it in your marriage, if you really have that big of an issue with it. You can just say, \"No, I don't want it,\" and that's it. But still you can find the marriage, and then you can live with a partner as a Muslim, and that person will teach you. There will be Community, there'll be friends. The world is a big place. It's much bigger than just a family and what people are around us do and what they say and what our parents teach us.", "It is a big jump, but it all depends on this: it is the Truth, so I accept it for the sake of God. Think about it, read the Quran, take your time. And ask God for Guidance. Ask God to keep you in the Truth and to open your heart to the Truth.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Lady Enquires About Heaven In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NyrpGRsef5I", ((2865, "47:45–48:18"), (2909, "48:29–49:05"),), id: 3560)
// U ML099:567-599 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("Islam is a practical religion. Allah sees you, and He knows what you can and cannot do. And He told us in the Quran (alBaqarah2:286) that He doesn't overburden us except that we can handle. You need to first build your faith, your Iman, focus on the important aspects, take your time, and then, when you're ready, take these decisions. This guilt-tripping is more something that Christianity uses 24/7: \"Oh, you're a sinner, this and that..\" It's NOT an Islamic thing! We have a reasonable understanding of what people can and cannot do. And Allah takes them a step by step.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Shockingly Describes Life After Death Like You Are Witnessing It! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lePF6KO1aZA", ((1627, "27:07–28:08"),), id: 3561)
// R quran_002_286.json
#refbox("Reference text: Quran 2:286, quran.com (Saheeh International)", (("2:286", "Allāh does not charge a soul except [with that within] its capacity. It will have [the consequence of] what [good] it has gained, and it will bear [the consequence of] what [evil] it has earned. \"Our Lord, do not impose blame upon us if we have forgotten or erred. Our Lord, and lay not upon us a burden like that which You laid upon those before us. Our Lord, and burden us not with that which we have no ability to bear. And pardon us; and forgive us; and have mercy upon us. You are our protector, so give us victory over the disbelieving people.\""),))
// U ML314:791-813 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("No one is perfect; there is not a Muslim on earth who's perfect. The Prophetﷺ told us: «كلُّ بني آدم خَطَّاءٌ، وخيرُ الخَطَّائِينَ التوابون» (Every child of Adam commits sins), and then he said (the best of the people who make sins are those who repent). The reality is that you got to repent from the sins that you do. You have to know that what you're doing is a sin, but you will fall, you will do sins.", "Now when you talk about the knowledge, no one is born knowing everything. I'm learning everyday about Islam, everyone is learning everyday about Islam. It is a gradual step-by-step process that people take. A person becomes Muslim, and he's not accountable for anything except that which he knows. So if you do something that is wrong but unknowingly, you're not accountable for it. It's a step-by-step process. That's why Allah, in the beginning of the mission of Prophetﷺ, did not make alcohol prohibited at once. It was a gradual process, because it was difficult for people: they were just drinking it more than water; it was the culture at the time. So things are gradually taken step by step.", "The important thing is to believe in the foundations of Islam: that there is One God worthy of worship, Jesus is a Messenger sent by God, he did not die for anyone's sins, because everyone is responsible for his own sins, no one takes the sin of someone else. He is coming, there's a second coming.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Does Jesus Possess The Attributes of God?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2Jp6DQffnZg", ((2406, "40:06–40:19"), (2426, "40:26–40:54"), (2454, "40:54–41:03"),), id: 3562)
// U ML155:291-309 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("The prophet, when he sent his companion [Muadh], that was the name of His companion, he sent him to Yemen, a country called Yemen. There was people of the book there, Christians and Jews. He said to them: \"You're going to invite a people of the book to Islam. Let the first thing you call them to is to worship [one] God Alone.\" That is the most important thing. The prophet said: \"If they agree, then tell them there's prayers. Then if they agree, then tell them they have to give charity\": the gradualism that we talk about. So the prophet didn't say: go tell them everything that they should and shouldn't do, which will confuse them. You have to take people gradually, step by step.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Intelligent Students Ask Curious Questions About Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XLWOnl9JFok", ((613, "10:13–10:46"),), id: 3563)
// U ML314:930-963 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("The last thing I do is to push people to take anything. You want to just investigate something, you want to read something, you want to check something, you can do whatever you want to do, and when you want to take that step, then take that step.", "What the brother needs to understand is: you accepting Islam is the most important thing; is that which saves you from Hellfire. Everyone commits sins on a daily basis. In order for the sister to feel like she's comfortably wearing the Hijab, she has to first enter into the fold of Islam, start practising, and then, when her Iman increases, she will want to do it on her own. Now as a husband, you have to understand that reverts have to take things step by step. You don't tell them to do this from the beginning, change your life 180 degrees. That's not the way things are done. They take their time, and you do reminders after a while, when you feel like she is more comfortable with it. You can remind her, that's it. You're not going to be a sinner for a wife not wearing the Hijab, even if you reminded her, because we do not force anyone. No one can force anyone to do anything in Islam.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Does Jesus Possess The Attributes of God?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2Jp6DQffnZg", ((2848, "47:28–47:39"), (2886, "48:06–48:40"),), id: 3564)
// U ML403:112-169 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("You're still a Muslim! You ask for forgiveness. And when you pray, you come close to Allah; then you will want to leave these things. Because you and me, we cannot just leave things like this. No one changes 360 degrees. I had a friend, he became Muslim. He used to drink. He's a heavy drinker; he's Irish. They drink it like water. He became Muslim, and he was drinking for six months after Islam. And then he left. It took him time, it will take you time, it will take everyone time. But you do it right now, and you don't delay it. You do it right now, you make your choice. And you're talking about a girlfriend: marriage is open. Try to find you a wife, to get a wife, instead of going that way.", "Prayer in Islam is our connection to Allah. If you're connected to Allah, you are in your strongest case. You will leave anything for Allah. But right now, you're not connected. You're disconnected from your Creator. That's why things will be difficult for you to leave. Shaytan will say what to you? \"Leave it, leave it, leave it, leave it..\" And he will always delay you more and say to you: \"Leave this first.\" Why? So you die! Once you die, he knows you're going to Hellfire; this is his plan. His plan is to make you die as a disbeliever. So you take the step today.", "Allahﷻ says in the Quran that if He wants to guide you, He will open your heart to Islam (alAn'am6:125). And Allahﷻ says that those who struggle in Our Way, We will make it easy for them (al'Ankabut29:69), We guide them to Our ways. So if you want Allah to make it easy for you, to open your doors for marriage, for this, for that, first take the step. When you take the step, you will be tested. Things will become difficult maybe in your life; you need to remain steadfast on your religion. And then Allah will open doors for you.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Emotional Shahada! Brother Accepts Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hvQ9biPlbos", ((228, "3:48–4:30"), (277, "4:37–5:19"), (325, "5:25–5:48"),), id: 3565)
