eam just so I can arrange a discussion with you, or have the viewer speak to you, so we can talk. What's the problem with doing that? Where's the argument there? Then you say you have a plan, you have plans to do in the stream. No worries. We don't need to talk in the stream. Where did I say let's talk today? And then you said I ended my stream after. Yes, because the purpose was, like I said, I saw you live. You've been making many posts. I've called you out on Twitter. You've ignored it. So I said okay, let's have a discussion. You refused to have a discussion. You avoided it. That's why I ended the stream.", "He pretended that he didn't have any clue what's going on, but he's clearly watching my stream. He opened my page, as he's saying, and he saw that I started the stream and he saw that I ended the stream. But he didn't accept the discussion. You didn't have to do it on that live stream. The point was to invite you to a discussion about Islam, about the things that you said. I have nothing against you. I have no problems with you, but I have problems with the claims that you've made about Islam.", "What does he keep repeating? I don't know who this guy is. I never heard of this guy. A year ago, some of our Dawa brothers went on his podcast or channel, and they had a debate with Christians. You will see him making a post and tagging my handle literally in the post and asking for a debate. So he's asking me to join, to represent the Muslim side against the Christian side in a debate, and he's literally tagging my handle, and then he doesn't know who I am. And by the way, that was the first time there was any type of interaction between me and him. He initiated it by literally mentioning me in his posts. So I DM'd him. Why would you pretend? If you don't want to have discussions, fine, but don't clearly lie, like you don't know who I am, when you mentioned my name yourself, and then after you did that I DM'd you, and then you literally in the DM say: are you that