#passage(("You already have a point of view that you want to demonstrate, but you're asking me the question to pretend that you're looking for an answer, but in reality, you just want to say what you have in your mind? Or is it that you're looking for an answer? Which one is it?", "Gaslighting doesn't work, by the way, and I will highlight it if you try to gaslight. You're speaking on my behalf. It's gaslighting, trying to say I'm shying away from the conversation.", "You are now, with all due respect, lying, because I said in the beginning, I'm not accusing you of doing that, but Christians do these shotgun tactics. I was very clear saying that. So don't accuse me of something I didn't say. I actually was very explicit saying, \"I'm not accusing YOU of that.\" So please don't misrepresent my position. I'm very careful about what I say. That's the first thing. The second thing, I was also very careful that you're allowed to ask two questions. And then I answered your question, and then you asked the question again. I repeated the answer again. Then you asked the question again. I repeated the answer again. And that's why I said we're not going to keep going in a circle of me repeating the same question hundreds of times. It's wasting my time and the viewers' time. I'm not here to debate. I'm here to answer questions.", "What did Imam Shafi'i say in his book [al-Umm] about this? There's no such thing as an encyclopedia of jurisprudence that Muslims take to be reliable. [Dorar.net]? I've never heard of this website in my life. When someone says I've studied the jurisprudence, that means they've opened the books of the Schools of Thought. I don't think you even know. Can you tell me the names of the 4 Schools of Thought of Islam, without Googling?", "You, God logic, you claim that you've studied Islamic jurisprudence on this subject, and you cannot even name the names of the 4 schools, which is the basic ABC. But you claim you know the positions of the four jurisprudence Schools of Thought that you don't know their full names on this matter! I'm showing to the viewers whether you're saying the truth or you're lying, because you claimed you studied the Schools of Thought, and the jurisprudence on this issue.", "The four Schools of Thought of Islam is not a website. The four Schools of Thought of Islam, before the existence of the Internet, and before websites were made: there are books written on the jurisprudence of the four Schools of Thought. Who is the founder of the website? How do you know he's giving you reliable information? You don't know! I'm criticising YOU, not him, because YOU are the one who made the claim you've done research, and it is not research when I Google something on a website and I don't even know who the founder is. If I did that with Christianity, or other religions, I'll be a mockery in the scenes of challenging and discussions. The reason being is: there are books that I open, like the book of the Bible itself. Not googling what the Bible says, but actually opening the Bible itself and reading it, reading the actual books of the Christian history, what the church fathers \"say\". This is how you learn. These are sources of information.", "Now, you do not even know who are the founders of the four Schools of Thought. You do not know the names of the Schools of Thought. You don't know the founders. You do not know the name of the books that they've written. And I can name all of them. The difference between someone who's done the research, actually, on this matter: I can tell you the names of the books, and the (Mu'tamad), meaning the opinion that is taken in the Madhab, and who wrote the book. That doesn't mean I'm boosting my knowledge in this issue, but I'm saying I'm not going to say I've done research unless I've ACTUALLY done research. And actually doing research is actually opening the SOURCES, the primary source material, not a website somewhere on Google that puts opinions based on what they think the Schools of Thought said.", "It's irrelevant for me what any website says, because I don't need to rely on websites. I've opened the materials themselves, the primary source materials. And what concerns every Muslim is what The Quran and Sunna say. So unless you bring me evidences from the Quran, from The Prophet's statements, like I gave you when I told you about the harm principle: I gave you a Hadith, a statement of The Prophetﷺ where that principle is derived from. This is how things work in the Quran and Sunnah. You bring the evidences from the Quran and Sunnah, and then you use them to demonstrate a position to be accurate or not accurate.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “God Logic Gets Absolutely Schooled After Confronting The Muslim Lantern Live! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=81jGHV8IgmY", ((1132, "18:52–19:02"), (1180, "19:40–19:47"), (1203, "20:03–20:55"), (1280, "21:20–22:19"), (1399, "23:19–24:28"), (1501, "25:01–26:10"), (1572, "26:12–26:48"), (1618, "26:58–27:23"),), id: 3683)
