#passage(("The reason why David wood makes claims like this is because he's trying to create a wedge between Muslims and their Scholars, and the audience in general and the [dawah] Bros or the [dawah] men. If you can cast doubt in regards to their credibility, then naturally you're going to reject everything they say, and you're going to stick with this alternative that David wood is presenting. And he's pretending like there's some sort of uniformity among scholars in all cases, as if these Scholars gather once a year in a basement somewhere and they come up with rulings or they come up with theories in order to deceive the masses. Well, here's the thing: if that was the case, then why is there so much division among the scholars, among the [du'at], among Muslims in general? They come from different schools, they have different theological views, they refute each other all the time.", "However, ironically, we find them all agreeing when it comes to matters like: does the Quran endorse and believe in the authority and preservation of the Bible? You don't find that happening; you find them constantly refuting that, which is of course a challenge that David himself failed when I've presented it to him in the past. So when you find the Muslim Scholars agreeing upon something and the Christian apologists like David disagreeing with them, that means it's most likely because the Christian Scholars or the Christian apologist are reading into it in a way that no one has read into it before due to their biases, or rather, in this specific case, it's because David wood is being disingenuous, because that's something that he himself has admitted to do.", "Another tactic that David wood is guilty [of] is pretending that nobody refutes his points even when they do. I've actually made the video about this specific Hadith, and David wood has butchered my position. Not only that, but I've broken down [the isnad] of the report and showed why it's something that you cannot rely upon. And that's not even the craziest part. The weirdest thing is that David has actually watched my video and he's reacted to it in a stream, and now he's butchering my position. So did David have some sort of Amnesia, or is it that David wood is being deceptive and intentionally misrepresenting my view?", "Some people for some reason do consider David wood to be a valid source of information about Islam, and there are two reasons why no one should view him as such. One is due to the tens of examples of blunders, and the second reason is because David himself has admitted that he intentionally puts the prophet, peace be upon him, in the worst possible light in order to get back at the Muslim. So he's admitting that he's being disingenuous.",), "Farid Responds, “David Wood Exposes Himself!!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mYKjUtvS46k", ((236, "3:56–4:54"), (296, "4:56–5:43"), (343, "5:43–7:29"), (485, "8:05–8:42"),), id: 3687)
