#passage(("I thought [Christian] Prince wasn't going to respond, and I waited a few days, and when he did respond, it wasn't what I expected. To give you guys a brief background of what's going on: he was acting as if he was a Muslim. He never says that he's not a Muslim; he says he's a muslim. This guy was faking being a Muslim, and he was on Christian Prince's show. So we made a video about that, and it got a good amount of views, and it put pressure on Christian Prince, because it opened the door to another question, which was: are all the people that leave Islam on Christian [Prince's] show fake?", "Now, there's something very important I'd like you guys to be aware of: nowhere in my interview with [Afzal] do we condemn Christian Prince for this, or accuse him of being in cahoots with the fake [Afzal]. We don't do that. I can't prove it, so I can't claim it. But it is a thought. It's something that's looming in my head, and I'm sure in the heads of most of you guys.",), "Farid Responds, “Does Christian Prince bring Fake Muslims on his Show?”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u1gomstItQU", ((10, "0:10–3:58"), (243, "4:03–4:33"),), id: 3727)
// U FR289:101-505 | Farid Responds | 9
#passage(("[Christian Prince], this Punk, makes this lengthy video where he makes several points, and here's the thing: he's enraged. He hated the fact that we made this video. Well, naturally, because it's not just questioning his credibility; we've attacked his credibility so many times. Alhamdulillah, I think I did a great job. And CP, who ignores other channels, isn't ignoring Mine. He's going after my videos, even my videos that aren't directed at him. He's so filled with hatred that he wants to get back at me. And I do understand, but CP, truly, there's only one person to blame, and that's yourself. If you don't lie, this wouldn't happen to you. If you weren't so vile, this wouldn't happen to you. If you didn't make dumb points, incompetent points, if you knew how to read good Arabic, if you know how to read English, I wouldn't be doing this, at least not at this level. I wouldn't be able to hurt your image so badly if you were competent, and I wouldn't be able to hurt your image so badly if you were truthful. So the only person that you have to blame, it's yourself.", "And there are other critics of Islam out there, and I'm not going after them, not because I can't; it's because you are the easiest Target. Inshallah, the others, they'll get their time. Others are much bigger: David Wood's a lot bigger than you. I made like two, three videos about him. How many videos I made about you? It's because you're so easy to deal with.", "Christian Prince made a video response about this, and there are a bunch of fallacies in this video. Again, he loses it. He's enraged by what's going on with [Afzal], and this in itself is extremely suspicious. Why is this suspicious? It's because, if I had a guest on my show and he was accused of being fake, and I didn't know if he was fake or not, if I didn't have proof, I would say, \"I don't know, guys. I'm not responsible for guys that come on my show. I'm not responsible for claims that they've made. I believe them, but if there's proof against what they've claimed, then I'm not [responsible], and I do apologize for bringing someone on my show that lied to you.\" That's what I would do. Christian Prince is not like that.", "Christian Prince, you wouldn't call me a son of [mut'ah] if we were to meet face to face, and that's why you enjoy being in your comfort zone, in your basement, behind the screen, cowering away in fear: because, one, you ain't going to get exposed publicly, and two, it's because you do not have [the cojones] to say any of this in my face.", "Notice: this guy left Islam on cp's show, and two minutes later says that he accepts Jesus, he accepts Jesus as God. \"Oh, Jesus did a lot of good things, therefore he must be God\"? This is ridiculous, and to be honest, this in itself is sufficient for anyone to doubt the story, this alone. But Subhan Allah, we actually found someone who is impersonating someone who actually knows him. It turned out to be someone I know.", "Now CP says that I need to bring video evidence. I need to drag this guy, I need to go to the school, because apparently [Afzal] and ex-Muslim fake [Afzal] have been in school for an extra 10 years or so, maybe more, and I'm supposed to say, \"Hey, excuse me, fake [Afzal], would you mind admitting on camera that you're fake? Would you mind apologizing to the audience?\" Is this a joke? CP, I have a question for you: when you put up a video, claimed that it was me, did you have video evidence that it was me? You put up a video of someone who sounded nothing like me, and you claimed that it was me, and that was sufficient evidence for you. That person didn't even refer to himself as [Farid]. That person sounded nothing like me, didn't have my name, and yet it was sufficient evidence for you. How come the double standards? I have something even better than video evidence for you.", "A couple of months ago, [Afzal] actually called Rob Christian, your little friend, and he went on his show. And by the way, CP, I do not understand how you could make fun of the way I talk, when this guy, Rob, is working with you, and you're making fun of my voice. So later on in the show, guess who? It's the same guy. Apparently he's a Christian.", "Let's review what we learned here. This Christian admits clearly that he has a relationship with [Afzal]: they've debated and they're in touch. Furthermore, [Afzal] sent him a message, a WhatsApp message, on the 20th of January, confirming what was said on Rob's show about [Al Imran] verse number 55. They had both debated in the past, and they both grew up in the same country, the Middle East. He also admits that he grew up as a Christian and had Muslims around him, which further corroborates [Afzal's] statements in the original video. Most importantly, the voices are a perfect match, one where he is a Christian and the other where he pretends to be a Muslim. And with that, the mystery of the fake [Afzal] is solved.", "A message to you, you Christian, you believer in Christ, you believer in all that's good and holy: you need to lie about Islam, this fake religion, this fake satanic religion in your eyes, you need to lie about Islam in order to prove Christianity? You need to be a fake Muslim that converts to Christianity on a live show in order to influence Muslims? Is that how low you are? You're a sad person. But hey, you're someone who looks up to CP, and what else am I supposed to expect? So shame on you. And there is a way of correcting this, and if you were someone who cared about the truth, you would do this: you would make a statement, you can send a statement audio, you say, \"Hey [Afzal], I'm sorry, I screwed up. I was being childish, I was being an idiot, I was being a fool. [Afzal], I'm sorry for impersonating you,\" that's one, \"and I'm sorry to the Muslims that had to see me stoop so low.\" That's what you should say. But I do not think that you have the honor to do such a thing.",), "Farid Responds, “Does Christian Prince bring Fake Muslims on his Show?”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u1gomstItQU", ((280, "4:40–6:06"), (366, "6:06–6:31"), (391, "6:31–7:38"), (458, "7:38–9:18"), (694, "11:34–12:10"), (839, "13:59–15:09"), (946, "15:46–18:59"), (1255, "20:55–21:59"), (1327, "22:07–24:13"),), id: 3728)

