#passage(("Today Christian Prince has uploaded a video celebrating his victory against me. We'll see how victorious he really was. Now I had previously made a video calling out Christian Prince for a misattribution. Of course I claim that this is an incorrect reference, since the page does not include this quote. He then made another video and provided a new reference, and not surprisingly that quote wasn't there either. I then challenged CP to produce the quote. I even said that I would make a public apology if he was able to find this quote.", "Your book says volume 1 page 282. The second reference that you provided after my initial video was volume 1 page 379, and now you provide a new reference: volume 6 page number 533.", "There is one question that comes to mind, and I will admit that I did not realize this before watching Christian Prince's latest video: why would Christian Prince provide an incorrect reference twice? He also said that he was quoting [al-Tanwir] instead of quoting [Fath al-Bari] directly. Now this is a very odd thing to do. You see, [Fath al-Bari] is perhaps the most famous hadith commentary in existence; [al-Tanwir] is an obscure source in comparison.", "Let's return to the original quote. In [al-Tanwir] it says: they said those who fear Allah will have a stronger libido. Now what does [Ibn Hajar] actually say? He says: it is said those who are more fearful will have a stronger libido. There is a major difference between the two statements. The former, without the context, implies that the [strong libido] is a supernatural occurrence. On the other hand, the latter suggests that there is an observable natural link between not falling into sins, like gazing at members of the opposite sex, and the libido. This opinion is supported by scientific research.", "Furthermore, [Ibn Hajar's] actual words do not exactly paint the sexual picture of Islam that Christian Prince was going for, and this is why he sought after the misquotation in the obscure [al-Tanwir].", "What should you expect from someone that has actively avoided a hundred and seven accusations that I've made against him? In regards to my apology: I'm sorry for all your fans that trust you after all the lies that you have fed them. I'm sorry for all the fans that know that you're a liar but still choose to support you. Most importantly, I feel sorry for the sad state of Christianity today, since it has to depend on someone so shallow, so vile and so despicable as yourself to represent it.",), "Farid Responds, “My Public Apology - Christian Prince”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lyQOTRfppGA", ((0, "0:00–0:55"), (72, "1:12–1:26"), (101, "1:41–2:21"), (169, "2:49–3:47"), (235, "3:55–4:12"), (259, "4:19–5:28"),), id: 3732)
