#passage(("I'm going to be going through Christian [Prince's] Sex and Allah. This guy actually takes pride in his works, and he's received a lot of great five-star reviews. I'm not going to go through this full thing. I'm just going to go through the first paragraph to show you the value of this work: \"Imam [al-Hafiz] and [Ibn Hajar] in the book said anyone he fear Allah Allah will make him extremely horny and this is was one of the privilege of the prophet may Allah pray on him and salute him. Therefore he used to do intercourse for all his women every day. Volume one page 282.\"", "So there are a bunch of issues here. First of all, what the heck is up with the third grade level of English? A major translation error in this paragraph comes in the form of \"he used to do intercourse for all his women every day\". The Arabic doesn't say that. It doesn't say every day. It says in a day.", "Other problems include the following. The first issue is that [al-Hafiz] and [Ibn Hajar] are actually the same person. Secondly, this opinion is not the opinion of [Ibn Hajar]; rather, \"they said\". Now I'm not sure who they are. However, it is false to attribute the statement to [Ibn Hajar]. Perhaps the biggest mistake here is the attribution of this quote to [Fath al-Bari] in the first place. You see, [Ibn Hajar's] book does not include any of this text. What I'd like to understand is why Christian Prince provided a page volume and number for this quote. Now keep in mind that this is the very first paragraph of this book. If I were to go through the full thing, I would have to make at least 100 videos.", "In conclusion: bad grammar, bad English, bad translation, deceptions, false referencing, and obvious ignorance of the subject, and we're just on the first paragraph of the book. Look at how many positive reviews this thing has. People are eating it up, thinking that this book is worth the $13 excluding shipping costs.",), "Farid Responds, “Christian Prince Book Review”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CIRrpHW8Dag", ((48, "0:48–1:43"), (103, "1:43–2:26"), (146, "2:26–3:26"), (208, "3:28–3:59"),), id: 3737)
