#passage(("There's so many Christian apologists that have been begging me for debates recently. I have presented to you the Christian dilemma: the Christians believe in their Bible even though their own Christian scholars agree to [its] corruption. Now many Muslims have been debating the ridiculous so-called dilemma, which is a defense position, where Muslims would debate and defend their so-called Islamic dilemma. We've seen many debates that have happened recently. Now let's see if there is one Christian who is willing to debate the Christian dilemma and tell us how Christians can follow their scriptures when their own Christian scholars say that it is corrupted.", "So who is willing to defend the corruption of the Bible? This is not about Islam. It's about Christianity. Who's willing to debate the Christian dilemma and defend their Bible from the scholarship of Christianity and from textual criticism from Christians and non-Christians? No attacking Islam; defending your religion, just like you were doing with those Muslims who are debating your so-called dilemma. The only thing you need if you're going to accept this challenge, which I know is not going to happen anyways, is that you have to be a respectful and respected Christian apologist or preacher. So no foulmouth individuals, people who are accused of rape or admitting to rape, or wife beaters. Respectful and respected Christians, and at least have 500 plus [subs].", "Here's the challenge for you: let's debate the Christian dilemma, and you defend your Bible. I'm going to present statements from your Christian scholars and from non-Christian scholars, and all you have to do is defend. Explain to us how do you believe in your book while your own scholars admit to its corruption. So I'm looking forward to no one accepting this challenge ever.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Christian Dilemma: Do Muslims Believe The Bible Is Corrupted? Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3bEZW_kx7Xg", ((6089, "1:41: