#passage(("Since Daniel wants to debate me so badly, I offered him the subject, and I outlined the question as follows: does the belief that the 12 imams possess control over all atoms in the universe constitute [shirk] Akbar if they are dependent on Allah? Daniel then responds by pretending that this was never his position. He also explained that there are three other definitions, so I asked him: when you said what you said in those clips defending this, which of the three positions were you referring to? And that was it; no more response. The video I released on the subject was all the way back in February, detailing his views. He couldn't deal with it, so he ignored it.", "I want to remind you that Daniel initially said a lot of Sunnis and Shia that believe in this, and now, by changing his definition of the term, pretending that it doesn't exist, he's absolving a lot of Sunnis, and the only reason he's doing this is to save his own reputation. You're pretending that all this doesn't exist in order to serve yourself. It's funny, though, because Daniel says that he's happy to debate me, but only on the positions that we agree upon. Why would you debate me on something that we agree upon? Daniel, the debate challenge is still available whenever you want to defend the belief that believing in 12 demigods is not [shirk] Akbar. I'm still here.", "You see, you could circumambulate around the grave. You can do [tawaf] around it. You could take the sand of the grave and wipe it on your face while believing that this person in the grave has control over all the atoms in the universe, and Daniel would rather condemn Muhammad [ibn Abd al-Wahhab] instead of educating you on the [shirk] that you're upon.",), "Farid Responds, “My Reaction to Wahhabism Video + Debate Challenge”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zfe0bjwAAl4", ((1186, "19:46–20:35"), (1239, "20:39–21:40"), (1318, "21:58–22:22"),), id: 3766)
