// U FR173:14-136 | Farid Responds | 4
#passage(("I gave you a chance, and you failed badly. I'm not running into rooms chasing you down, seeking a debate with you. You're trying to save face, because that last back and forth ended badly. That's why the video is up on my channel; it's not up on yours. You need to learn to be charitable.", "Here's what he's speaking about. I said I have nothing to gain from debating him, in the same way that for someone like Ahmad Shawani, who's a very popular [Shia] speaker, he has nothing to gain from debating me. And what do I mean by that? I don't mean [Ahmad] is going to be making money or anything like that, but when I say \"has nothing to gain\", it means he's only going to make me a bigger name. And here's the thing: if I destroy [Ahmad], it's going to hurt him, right? But if [Ahmad Shawani] destroys me, no one really cares, because Ahmad is such a big name. When I destroyed Said Ali, they don't care; it doesn't make a difference. But if Said Ali were to destroy me: \"Oh wow, who's the Ali guy who destroyed [Farid]?\" That's the thing.", "I say to Ali: even though I did admit that you're someone that has been doing this for 10 years, a lot of people, they're like: \"This guy's a nobody, this guy's a layman, this guy doesn't know the definition.\" I received DMs; the mods were receiving DMs that you don't know the meaning of the term. That's the issue. I have nothing to gain from debating you. Someone on Twitter was saying that [you're] target practice. So I can't do this. I gave you a chance to take it back. He insisted to stick to his false opinion that [mutawatir] is two people, and Shiites were ridiculing this. I think it was big of me to give you a second chance to take it back, but you took the L. I'm not going to give you another chance.", "The guy is claiming that I'm doing this for my ego. I don't make a single dollar from any of my content on YouTube or anything like that, and I really believe that anyone that does this for his ego, that does this for subs, does any of this for fame, this is a disease in itself.",), "Farid Responds, “Debate Aftermath”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9FoxqMRTV6s", ((66, "1:06–2:28"), (167, "2:47–3:49"), (229, "3:49–4:54"), (296, "4:56–5:25"),), id: 3768)
