#passage(("We're here to actually go through these quotes, because I have examples of you taking things out of context; I have examples of lying. If you actually go to the link and you scroll down to where it says \"my references\", you will actually find the references I provided in the footnotes.", "If one of your students provided sources this way and just said \"you go do your homework\", what would you do? You actually start from a snapshot of half a sentence, and then sentences that show no page number, no book, no work, no reference that you can actually go to. That's how you provide sources?",), "Farid Responds, “Debate with Minhaji”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1Yk6e4IZGmM", ((699, "11:39–12:32"), (957, "15:57–16:17"),), id: 3769)
// U FR144:634-708 | Farid Responds | 2
#passage(("After Minhaji leaves, I asked folks to invite him back again if he'd like to continue, but Minhajji never came back. So what we did do was we did go through the rest of the alleged quotations. We went through them one by one, and we provided examples of manipulation and misquotation. There were some quotes where I'd say \"give us a source\", and he would say \"you didn't do your homework\". You see, that's the issue: when someone asks for a reference, you just give them the reference. You don't say \"you didn't do your homework\". Where the hell am I supposed to look? I used search features to look up some of the stuff that he's quoting. I simply couldn't find it. How could I be blamed if he's too incompetent and he just simply doesn't know how to provide proper referencing?", "The reason why I felt the necessity to do this is to simply expose this fraud for the type of person that he is, and his manipulation of the statements of the scholars of hadith, because it's something I really care about. And yes, there is an agenda, because the whole reason why he weakened [Asim] is because [Asim narrates] a hadith he doesn't like, has to do with attributes of Allah. He's turning this thing into a Salafi versus Ashari [thing], and it's not supposed to be. We're speaking about a narrator, and this guy's manipulating evidence.",), "Farid Responds, “Debate with Minhaji”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1Yk6e4IZGmM", ((1910, "31:50–33:08"), (2006, "33:26–34:11"),), id: 3770)
// U FR233:489-535 | Farid Responds | 1
#passage(("This is what you have to pay attention to when you're tossed these lists: there's always something going on. You are trying to have a civil, respectful conversation with someone; he tosses you a list of sources. They're usually not interested in a civil, respected dialogue; they just want to shut you up. Is that how you win an argument, by giving your intellectual opponent so many sources that they just give up? No. You win an argument by presenting one point; the other side examines it, and they provide their response, and you have a discussion. That's how discussions are supposed to be held; that's how dialogues are supposed to be held. This is childish, when someone just tosses everything and the kitchen sink at you, trying to sink you. I went through your 31 points, responded to all 31. The least you can do is respond to my one point.",), "Farid Responds, “Debunking Shia Claim: Abu Bakr and Omar killed Fatima!! [Mahdi Modarresi]”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u92BmUM3rxM", ((1227, "20:27–21:52"),), id: 3771)
// U FR166:34-123 | Farid Responds | 2
#passage(("A couple of months ago I was on Clubhouse, and this individual comes onto the room I was in, jumps on the panel, starts asking me questions; he records it and he uploads onto his channel. I don't care; all is fair; you can go ahead, upload whatever you like. But he came back a while later, and we had this lengthy debate, and he didn't do too well, and the debate was recorded, and some guys sent it to me. Apparently he looked quite bad in it, even though he claimed that he did well, and he looked so bad that he's going to YouTube and complaining, saying that there's private information in the video, so please, YouTube, take it down. Now what's funny here is there is no private information. It's just a discussion. No one's getting doxxed. It's just audio. The debate hurt his reputation; that's pretty much it, and he wants to see it gone.", "Now you know what you could have done? You could have contacted me directly, through YouTube comments, through Twitter, whatever. You could have just said: \"Hey Farid, I see you've uploaded the video. I feel like I didn't do too well in it, and perhaps it hurt my reputation. I would like for you to take the video down if you don't mind\", and I probably would have. But now that you've went this route, which again is quite hypocritical, since you are uploading clips of mine from those discussions, and you're not even uploading full clips, you're uploading portions, unfortunately the video is staying up.",), "Farid Responds, “He's trying to REMOVE my videos!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m1Z03W4-xiw", ((62, "1:02–2:44"), (168, "2:48–3:54"),), id: 3772)
